E["item:gnoam-sprecklesprocket"] = {t="item",n="Gnoam Sprecklesprocket",z="deadmines",s="The Gnoam Sprecklesprocket is a sophisticated power supply salvaged from Sneed's shredder deep within the Deadmines. Gnomish engineers seek this component to supercharge specialized drilling machines in an ambitious bid to reclaim their fallen home of Gnomeregan.",h="The Gnoam Sprecklesprocket is a sophisticated power supply salvaged from Sneed's shredder deep within the...",sec={{t="A Vital Power Source",b="Though manufactured or modified by goblins working alongside the Defias Brotherhood, the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket represents an exceptional feat of compact mechanical energy. Operating deep in the lumbering machine piloted by the goblin taskmaster Sneed, this specialized core delivers enough sustained energy to drive heavy industrial logging and cutting blades. Its stability and potent output make it an invaluable piece of salvage amidst the subterranean tunnels of Westfall.",sp=0},{t="Breaching Gnomeregan",b="In Stormwind City, the gnomish inventor Shoni the Shilent singled out the Deadmines shredder as the key to a larger offensive. Gnomish forces seek to reclaim Gnomeregan from the trogg hordes that overran it, but the sealed underground approaches present a formidable barrier. By harnessing the Sprecklesprocket, Shoni intends to power heavy gyrodrillmatic excavationators capable of boring directly through the solid bedrock surrounding the lost techno-city, establishing an unexpected underground assault route.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket?",a="It is an intact, high-output mechanical power supply extracted from a goblin shredder found deep in the Deadmines. It possesses enough output to run heavy underground drilling apparatus.",al={"sprecklesprocket","what is this sprocket","what is the item"},it="identity"},{q="Where does the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket come from?",a="It is recovered from Sneed's Shredder, an industrial lumber machine operated by the goblin taskmaster Sneed inside the lumber mills of the Deadmines.",al={"who drops it","how to get sprecklesprocket","shredder drop"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Shoni the Shilent need it?",a="Shoni requires its energy output to power gyrodrillmatic excavationators. These machines are designed to bore through the subterranean rock borders of Gnomeregan to allow Alliance-aligned gnomes to mount an assault against the troggs.",al={"why does shoni want this","shoni quest item"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Is the sprocket goblin or gnomish technology?",a="It is recovered from a functional goblin shredder in the Deadmines, and Shoni plans to use its power supply in gnomish drilling machinery. The source does not identify who originally designed the component.",al={"is it goblin tech","gnome or goblin device"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Every salvaged component brings the exiled gnomes closer to drilling into their lost home and driving out the trogg infestation.",["profession:Engineering"]="The sprocket is an intact power supply capable of powering the machinery needed to bore through Gnomeregan's rocky underground borders."},kw={"deadmines","gnoam sprecklesprocket","gnomeregan","gyrodrillmatic","shoni the shilent","sneed","sneed's shredder","sprecklesprocket"},rel={"quest:2040","npc:sneed-s-shredder","npc:shoni-the-shilent","npc:sneed","zone:deadmines","zone:gnomeregan","topic:trogg","topic:gnome"},src={"Gnoam Sprecklesprocket","Underground Assault"}}
E["item:head-of-vancleef"] = {t="item",n="Head of VanCleef",z="deadmines",s="The severed head of Edwin VanCleef serves as grim, irrefutable proof that the leader of the Defias Brotherhood has fallen. Brought back from the depths of the Deadmines to Sentinel Hill, it represents the hard-won vengeance of the People's Militia.",h="The severed head of Edwin VanCleef serves as grim, irrefutable proof that the leader of the Defias...",sec={{t="Proof of the Master's Fall",b="For months, Edwin VanCleef directed the Defias Brotherhood's terror from the deepest sanctum of the Deadmines, shielded by heavily armed outlaws, goblin engineers, and a massive war juggernaut. Words alone could never convince the battered settlers of Westfall that their nightmare was over. Gryan Stoutmantle, leader of the People's Militia, demanded undeniable physical proof before declaring the countryside safe. Severing the ringleader's head and bringing it out into the daylight offers the exhausted defenders tangible assurance that the grand architect of their ruin will never threaten Westfall again.",sp=0},{t="A Grim Victory",b="Though Stoutmantle sought VanCleef's death for the greater good of Westfall, presenting the trophy carries a heavy solemnity. VanCleef was once the revered master builder who rebuilt Stormwind after the First War, before betrayal and unpaid debts drove him and the Stonemasons Guild into outlaw rebellion. His severed head marks the culmination of Westfall's local militia campaign, yet it also exposes the kingdom's failure to handle its own domestic turmoil, leaving volunteer farmers and foreign adventurers to execute high justice.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who wants the Head of VanCleef?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle, captain of the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill in Westfall, requires the head to complete the long Defias Brotherhood campaign.",al={"who do i turn this into","who takes vancleef head","where does vancleef head go"}},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle demand his head specifically?",a="The Defias Brotherhood held a stranglehold over Westfall for so long that rumors of VanCleef's demise would never be believed without absolute physical proof. Stoutmantle needs unmistakable evidence to reassure the beleaguered farmers and show the militia's struggle was not in vain.",al={"why take his head","why vancleef head"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the head obtained?",a="It is taken from Edwin VanCleef aboard his secret ironclad warship, found at the very end of the Deadmines beneath Moonbrook in southwestern Westfall.",al={"where to get vancleef head","how to get head of vancleef"},it="origin"},{q="Does taking VanCleef's head end the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Stoutmantle views his death as the beginning of the end for the brotherhood, but splinter groups, rogue bandits, and sympathizers still linger throughout Westfall, Elwynn Forest, and beyond.",al={"is defias destroyed","what happens to the defias"}},{q="What is the Head of VanCleef?",a="The Head of VanCleef is the severed head of Edwin VanCleef, the mastermind behind the Defias Brotherhood hiding deep inside the Deadmines. It serves as gruesome, indisputable proof that the leader of the outlaw uprising has finally been brought down.",al={"what is head of vancleef","head of vancleef item","edwin vancleef head"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Presenting VanCleef's head provides a cathartic victory for the People's Militia, though it highlights the troubling absence of the Stormwind House of Nobles during Westfall's darkest hour.",["class:Rogue"]="Edwin VanCleef was one of the deadliest rogue masters in human history; taking his head marks the definitive end to a peerless career in shadows and sabotage."},kw={"deadmines","edwin vancleef","gryan stoutmantle","head of vancleef","peoples militia","sentinel hill","westfall"},rel={"npc:edwin-vancleef","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","quest:65","zone:deadmines","zone:westfall","topic:defias-brotherhood","quest:12","topic:alliance"},src={"Head of VanCleef","The Defias Brotherhood (7)"}}
E["item:miners-union-card"] = {t="item",n="Miners' Union Card",z="deadmines",s="A Miners' Union Card is an identification credential once carried by laborers working the rich subterranean veins beneath Moonbrook. Following a catastrophic cave-in that sealed a wing of the tunnels, these tokens now remain on the restless skeletal corpses wandering the dark drifts.",h="A Miners' Union Card is an identification credential once carried by laborers working the rich subterranean...",sec={{t="Tragedy in the Deep",b="Long before the Defias Brotherhood took absolute control over Moonbrook, laborers toiled underground under the banner of the miners' guild, extracting valuable ore for the kingdom. That ended in disaster when a severe tunnel collapse crushed a major shaft, trapping and killing dozens of workers beneath tons of rock. Rather than finding a quiet grave, those who perished rose again as skeletal miners, excavators, and dynamiters. The union cards clutched in their bony pockets are the sole surviving proof of their identities, sought out by surviving colleagues in Stormwind hoping to bring closure to grieving families.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Miners' Union Card?",a="It is an official identification card belonging to a member of the guild that once excavated the Moonbrook mines. Surviving workers use these cards to confirm who perished in the underground disaster.",al={"what is union card","miners card","union card"},it="identity"},{q="Where do these cards come from?",a="They are recovered from the undead laborers—such as skeletal miners, undead excavators, and undead dynamiters—haunting the collapsed drifts inside the Deadmines tunnels above Moonbrook.",al={"where to find union cards","who drops miners cards","card drop location"},it="origin"},{q="Why are the miners undead?",a="A catastrophic cave-in sealed them alive in a deep shaft. The dark, tainted atmosphere of the abandoned shafts prevented their souls from resting, binding their reanimated skeletons to reenact their final working hours.",al={"why skeletal miners","how did miners die","deadmines undead"}},{q="Who wants these cards returned?",a="Surviving co-workers who escaped the cave-in now reside in Stormwind City, collecting the cards so they can notify the families of the fallen and grant them peace.",al={"who takes union cards","collecting memories questgiver","turn in union cards"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="For prospectors and pickaxe wielders, the cards serve as a grim reminder of the deadly risks of subterranean cave-ins and unmanaged mine shafts.",["faction:Alliance"]="Recovering these lost tokens provides closure to families across the kingdom of Stormwind who never learned the true fate of their working kin."},kw={"cave-in","collecting memories","deadmines","miners' union card","moonbrook","skeletal miner","stormwind","union card"},rel={"quest:168","subzone:deadmines","zone:deadmines","subzone:moonbrook","zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Miners' Union Card","Collecting Memories"}}
E["item:thistlenettle-s-badge"] = {t="item",n="Thistlenettle's Badge",z="deadmines",s="Thistlenettle's Badge is an official insignia of the dwarven Explorers' League, once carried proudly by Foreman Thistlenettle into the depths of the Deadmines. Following a catastrophic cave-in and an invasion of thieves and the restless dead, the token is all that remains to confirm the foreman's tragic fate to his surviving brother in Stormwind.",h="Thistlenettle's Badge is an official insignia of the dwarven Explorers' League, once carried proudly by...",sec={{t="The Explorers' League in the Deadmines",b="Before the Defias Brotherhood locked down Moonbrook and the cavernous tunnels beneath it, dwarven prospectors affiliated with Ironforge's Explorers' League delved into the old gold mines of Westfall. Foreman Thistlenettle and his crew worked deep underground until a sudden tunnel collapse separated the team. While his brother Wilder managed to escape to Stormwind City, the foreman and several laborers remained trapped in the subterranean dark.",sp=0},{t="A Grim Confirmation",b="Rather than finding an honorable burial or an avenue of escape, Foreman Thistlenettle succumbed to the dark perils festering within the unsealed tunnels, rising as a mindless undead monstrosity among the collapsed shafts outside the main foundry. His Explorers' League Badge remained clutched upon his person, serving as the sole irrefutable proof of his death when recovered and delivered to his grieving brother.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who does this badge belong to?",a="The badge belonged to Foreman Thistlenettle, a dwarven miner and member of the Explorers' League who was trapped deep underground beneath Westfall during a sudden tunnel collapse.",al={"who owned thistlenettle badge","thistlenettle badge owner"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the badge found?",a="It is recovered directly from the undead remains of Foreman Thistlenettle, who wanders the monster-infested upper corridors of the Deadmines just outside the primary threshold of the Defias stronghold.",al={"badge location","how to get thistlenettles badge","where to find thistlenettle"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants Thistlenettle's Badge?",a="The badge is brought to Wilder Thistlenettle, the foreman's brother, who currently resides in the Dwarven District of Stormwind City awaiting word of his kin's fate.",al={"who takes thistlenettles badge","who turns in oh brother","wilder thistlenettle location"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why were the Thistlenettle brothers in the Deadmines?",a="The brothers were surveying and prospecting the extensive mineral-rich caverns beneath Moonbrook under the auspices of the Explorers' League before hostile thieves and structural collapses ruined their expedition.",al={"why were dwarves in deadmines","thistlenettle deadmines mission"},it="history"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Foreman Thistlenettle carried the banner and badge of the Explorers' League into Westfall; reclaiming his badge ensures a fallen son of Ironforge is not forgotten to the dark.",["faction:Alliance"]="Recovering this insignia brings closure to a grieving dwarf dwelling within Stormwind's Dwarven District."},kw={"deadmines","explorers' league","moonbrook","oh brother","thistlenettle","thistlenettle's badge","westfall","wilder"},rel={"quest:167","npc:foreman-thistlenettle","npc:wilder-thistlenettle","zone:deadmines","subzone:moonbrook","topic:explorers-league","zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Thistlenettle's Badge","Oh Brother. . ."}}
E["npc:captain-greenskin"] = {t="npc",n="Captain Greenskin",z="deadmines",s="Captain Greenskin is an elite goblin pirate overseeing the construction and crew of Edwin VanCleef's massive ironclad juggernaut. Hidden deep in the subterranean cove of the Deadmines, he commands the pirate forces hired by the Defias Brotherhood. His goal is to bring the warship to readiness to sail against Stormwind.",h="Captain Greenskin is an elite goblin pirate overseeing the construction and crew of Edwin VanCleef's massive...",sec={{t="Master of the Juggernaut",b="Pacing the main deck of the gigantic juggernaut under construction in the Deadmines cove, Captain Greenskin represents the naval backbone of the Defias conspiracy. A seasoned goblin mariner who previously operated out of Booty Bay, Greenskin was brought into Edwin VanCleef's inner circle to turn an underground cavern into a drydock for an engine of war.",sp=0},{t="A Pirate's Crew",b="Greenskin does not command an ordinary crew of stonemasons or bandits. Under his direct watch serve seasoned cutthroats, including his fearsome tauren first mate Mr. Smite and the murloc ship's cook, Cookie. Together, they hold the ship's gangplanks and upper deck, standing between intruders and VanCleef's private cabin atop the bridge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Greenskin?",a="Captain Greenskin is a goblin pirate captain hired by Edwin VanCleef to supervise the completion and operation of the Defias Brotherhood's secret war juggernaut in the Deadmines.",al={"greenskin lore","who is greenskin","captain greenskin"},it="identity"},{q="Where did Greenskin come from before joining the Defias?",a="Greenskin originally hails from Booty Bay in the southern reaches of Stranglethorn Vale, where he formerly commanded a fleet of pirate vessels before entering VanCleef's pay.",al={"greenskin origin","where is greenskin from","greenskin booty bay"},it="origin"},{q="Who serves under Captain Greenskin?",a="His command includes his first mate, the tauren Mr. Smite, as well as Cookie the murloc cook and a contingent of Defias pirates patrolling the ironclad's deck.",al={"greenskin crew","first mate","greenskin minions"},it="ties"},{q="What is Greenskin's purpose in the Deadmines?",a="He is tasked with making the massive ironclad warship seaworthy and prepared to sail out of the subterranean grotto into the Great Sea to strike at the kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"what does greenskin do","why is greenskin here"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can Captain Greenskin be found?",a="He paces the main deck of the large juggernaut anchored in the final cavern of the Deadmines, guarding the approach to Edwin VanCleef.",al={"greenskin location","where is captain greenskin"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is Captain Greenskin part of the Defias Brotherhood or a mercenary?",a="He is a mercenary pirate captain in the direct employ of Edwin VanCleef, commanding the naval forces aligned with the Defias Brotherhood's plot.",al={"is greenskin defias","greenskin faction"},it="side"},{q="Why is Captain Greenskin here?",a="Captain Greenskin was hired by Edwin VanCleef to oversee the construction and command of the Defias Brotherhood's massive juggernaut. He remains aboard the vessel deep within the Deadmines cove, directing his pirate crew and making sure the warship is completed and armed.",al={"why is greenskin in deadmines","captain greenskin why here","greenskin deadmines purpose"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="What does Captain Greenskin want?",a="As a hired goblin captain, Greenskin seeks profit and the thrill of naval command. He intends to finish constructing the colossal ironclad warship in the Deadmines cove and captain it out into the Great Sea in service to Edwin VanCleef's schemes against Stormwind.",al={"greenskin goal","what does captain greenskin want","greenskin motive"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Captain Greenskin feared?",a="Hailing from Booty Bay, Captain Greenskin formerly commanded an entire fleet of pirate vessels before entering VanCleef's employ. He is widely notorious among sailors as a ruthless veteran corsair, commanding brutal raiders like Mr. Smite with ironfisted discipline.",al={"why is greenskin feared","captain greenskin reputation","is greenskin famous"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance forces, Captain Greenskin represents the maritime threat of the Defias rebellion; if his juggernaut breaches the coast, the undefended shores of Westfall and Stormwind are at direct risk.",["class:Rogue"]="Greenskin stands at the apex of Defias piracy, heavily guarded by corsairs and brutes right on the warship's deck."},kw={"booty bay","captain greenskin","deadmines","goblin pirate","greenskin","juggernaut","smite","vancleef"},rel={"npc:edwin-vancleef","npc:mr-smite","npc:cookie","zone:deadmines","subzone:booty-bay","topic:pirate","topic:goblin","topic:alliance"},src={"Captain Greenskin"}}
E["npc:cookie"] = {t="npc",n="Cookie",z="deadmines",s="Cookie is an elite murloc serving as the ship's cook aboard the juggernaut hidden deep within the Deadmines. An unusual recruit among the Defias Brotherhood, he tends the crew's cauldrons beneath the watchful eye of Captain Greenskin and Edwin VanCleef. He is the only entirely optional boss encountered within the underground dry dock.",h="Cookie is an elite murloc serving as the ship's cook aboard the juggernaut hidden deep within the Deadmines.",sec={{t="The Brotherhood's Chef",b="Beneath the decks of the towering juggernaut in the Ironclad Cove, cooking duty falls neither to a human outrider nor a goblin engineer, but to a solitary murloc known simply as Cookie. How he secured the position remains a private secret kept by Edwin VanCleef himself. Whatever doubts the rest of the crew might harbor about a murloc presiding over their rations, pirates are rarely in a position to be picky, and in the underworld of Moonbrook, a meal is a meal.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Brew",b="Cookie patrols the waterways and shores around the pirate flagship, wielding his cooking utensils alongside acidic brews. Despite being isolated from typical murloc tribes, he defends his cauldron with savage ferocity, flinging caustic concoctions at any intruders who wander into the docks. Because his station sits away from the main gangplanks, many who storm the cove bypass his kitchen entirely, making him the only optional overseer aboard the Defias juggernaut.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is a murloc working as a cook for the Defias?",a="Edwin VanCleef is the only one who knows why Cookie was recruited and granted the galley duties. The Defias outlaws and goblin shipwrights simply accept the arrangement because pirate crews take food where they can get it, regardless of the chef's species.",al={"why murloc cook","why is cookie on the ship","cookie defias lore"},it="why_here"},{q="Where can Cookie be found in the Deadmines?",a="Cookie is located in the Ironclad Cove at the very end of the Deadmines. He patrols the shallow water and docks near the stern of the giant wooden juggernaut, just past the ramp where Mr. Smite stands guard.",al={"where is cookie","cookie location deadmines","finding cookie"},gp=true},{q="Is Cookie required to finish the Deadmines?",a="No, Cookie is the only optional boss in the dungeon. Infiltrators can board the vessel directly to confront Captain Greenskin and Edwin VanCleef without ever disturbing the cook's patrol along the shore.",al={"is cookie optional","do you have to kill cookie","cookie skip"},gp=true},{q="Does Cookie belong to a specific murloc tribe?",a="Cookie is not associated with any of the known local murloc tribes, such as those along the Westfall coast. He lives and works entirely among the outlaws and scoundrels of the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"what tribe is cookie","cookie murloc tribe"},it="origin"},{q="What weapons or attacks does Cookie use?",a="Cookie wields cooking implements in melee combat and can hurl caustic splashes of acid at attackers, burning them with dangerous culinary mixtures.",al={"cookie abilities","how does cookie fight","cookie attacks"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Who does Cookie report to on the juggernaut?",a="Cookie directly serves the naval arm of the Defias Brotherhood under the command of Captain Greenskin, answering ultimately to Edwin VanCleef himself.",al={"cookie boss","who leads cookie","cookie greenskin vancleef"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Cookie?",a="Cookie is an elite murloc serving as the ship's cook aboard Edwin VanCleef's ironclad juggernaut deep within the Deadmines. Unlike most feral murlocs encountered wandering the shores of Westfall, Cookie has found an unusual home among human outlaws, preparing questionable meals over his cauldron for the Defias Brotherhood's pirate crew.",al={"who is cookie","cookie identity","who is the murloc chef"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Cookie on?",a="Cookie is firmly loyal to the Defias Brotherhood. Stationed on the juggernaut alongside Captain Greenskin and Edwin VanCleef, he serves the outlaw pirates directly and will fiercely defend the ship against any Alliance intruders seeking to disrupt VanCleef's rebellion.",al={"cookie allegiance","is cookie defias","what faction is cookie"},it="side",add=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Finding a murloc appointed as chief cook aboard an outlaw juggernaut is a testament to the desperate, unrefined standards of pirate cuisine.",["class:Rogue"]="VanCleef's rogue network relies on strange, unconventional assets, and Cookie proves that even the Brotherhood's supply lines feature odd surprises.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind's scouts are often surprised to find murlocs actively working within the Defias leadership rather than merely infesting Westfall's outer shores."},kw={"captain greenskin","cook","cookie","deadmines","defias","edwin vancleef","ironclad cove","juggernaut","murloc"},rel={"npc:captain-greenskin","npc:edwin-vancleef","npc:mr-smite","zone:deadmines","topic:murloc","topic:pirate"},src={"Cookie"}}
E["npc:edwin-vancleef"] = {t="npc",n="Edwin VanCleef",z="deadmines",s="Edwin VanCleef was the brilliant Guildmaster of the Stonemasons who rebuilt Stormwind City after the Second War. After being cheated of payment by the House of Nobles, he led a violent workers' revolt and formed the outlaw Defias Brotherhood. Operating from deep within the Deadmines of Westfall, he seeks vengeance against the kingdom he helped restore.",h="Edwin VanCleef was the brilliant Guildmaster of the Stonemasons who rebuilt Stormwind City after the Second...",sec={{t="Architect of the Kingdom",b="Following the devastation of the First War, Edwin VanCleef was chosen to lead the Stonemasons Guild in the monumental task of rebuilding Stormwind City. A peerless craftsman and an idealist, VanCleef directed the construction of the capital's grand ramparts and towering cathedrals, and even oversaw the erection of Nethergarde Keep to watch over the Dark Portal. Alongside his mastery of architecture, VanCleef was a remarkably deadly operative; he was trained in stealth, subterfuge, and bladecraft by his childhood friend, Mathias Shaw.",sp=0},{t="The Riot and the Brotherhood",b="When the years of labor concluded, the House of Nobles ran up colossal debts through military campaigns and refused to provide the Stonemasons their promised compensation. Enraged, VanCleef demanded restitution, only for the nobles to officially dissolve the guild. The artisans revolted, triggering chaotic street riots in Stormwind during which King Varian Wrynn's wife, Queen Tiffin, was slain. Driven out of the capital by the crown's retribution, VanCleef gathered his exiled workers and allied outcasts in Westfall, uniting them beneath the banner of the Defias Brotherhood.",sp=0},{t="Retribution from the Shadows",b="Taking advantage of the crown's neglect of the countryside, the Defias drove off Westfall's farmers and claimed its rich gold deposits. Within the depths of Moonbrook's Deadmines, VanCleef oversaw the construction of a massive juggernaut warship, preparing an armed assault against Stormwind itself. While the House of Nobles dismissed the thieves as disorganized brigands, VanCleef forged alliances with river crooks, gnolls, and the Bloodsail Buccaneers, turning an embittered labor union into an army poised to crush the monarchy.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Edwin VanCleef?",a="He is the mastermind behind the Defias Brotherhood and the former Guildmaster of the Stonemasons. He is the master architect who rebuilt Stormwind City after the Horde destroyed it during the First War.",al={"who is vancleef","edwin vancleef lore","vancleef identity"},it="identity"},{q="Why did the Stonemasons revolt against Stormwind?",a="After the rebuilding of Stormwind City, the House of Nobles refused to pay the Stonemasons Guild their agreed wages due to excessive kingdom debt. When VanCleef and the workers protested, the nobles disbanded the guild, igniting violent riots in the streets.",al={"why did defias rebel","why did stonemasons riot","reason for defias riot"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is Edwin VanCleef hiding?",a="He commands the Defias Brotherhood from the innermost sanctum of the Deadmines in Westfall, whose entrance is rumored to lie through the quiet village of Moonbrook.",al={"where is vancleef","vancleef location","deadmines boss location"},sp=1,it="why_here"},{q="What is his connection to Mathias Shaw?",a="Mathias Shaw was a childhood friend of Edwin. Shaw personally trained VanCleef in the arts of stealth, thievery, and combat, originally hoping VanCleef would join him in the royal intelligence agency SI:7.",al={"vancleef and shaw","is vancleef related to shaw","mathias shaw friend"},it="ties"},{q="What happened to Queen Tiffin during the riot?",a="During the chaotic street riots stirred by the unpaid Stonemasons, a hurled stone struck and killed King Varian's young wife, Queen Tiffin Wrynn. Her death drove King Varian into a furious crackdown, forcing VanCleef and his men to flee the city.",al={"how did tiffin die","who killed tiffin wrynn","queen tiffin death"},it="history"},{q="What is he building in the Deadmines?",a="Rumor has it that the Defias have conscripted clever goblins to help them build something terrible at the bottom of the Deadmines, but what it may be is still uncertain.",al={"deadmines ship","what is inside deadmines","vancleef warship"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Edwin VanCleef on?",a="Edwin VanCleef stands solely with the Defias Brotherhood, the rebel syndicate he founded from the outcasts of the former Stonemasons Guild. He opposes both the House of Nobles and the crown of Stormwind, holding the entire kingdom responsible for breaking faith with his craftsmen. He owes no loyalty to the Alliance or the Horde, operating as an outlaw mastermind bent on pursuing his own fierce war of vengeance.",al={"edwin vancleef allegiance","who does edwin vancleef fight for","is vancleef alliance or horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Edwin VanCleef want?",a="VanCleef seeks total retribution against the Kingdom of Stormwind. After spending years rebuilding the capital city only to have the corrupt House of Nobles refuse payment and strip the Stonemasons Guild of their livelihood, he swore that the entire kingdom would pay for their betrayal. He aims to breach the city's defenses, crush the aristocracy, and exact vengeance for his exiled craftsmen through armed rebellion and open devastation.",al={"vancleef goal","what is edwin vancleef's goal","why is vancleef attacking stormwind"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Edwin VanCleef so feared?",a="Stormwind considers VanCleef one of the greatest perils to its security because he combines brilliant architectural knowledge with lethal rogue training. Having designed the very fortifications protecting the capital, he knows every vulnerability in the kingdom's defenses. Backed by a vast, cutthroat criminal network and heavily fortified within the Deadmines, he commands enough firepower, manpower, and cunning to bring the boy-king's realm to its knees.",al={"why is vancleef famous","why is edwin vancleef feared","edwin vancleef threat"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, VanCleef embodies the tragedy of the kingdom's postwar recovery: a loyal hero whose denied livelihood turned him into the realm's deadliest insurgent.",["class:Rogue"]="VanCleef was trained by SI:7 leader Mathias Shaw himself, making him one of the most capable rogues in Azeroth, blending formal guild leadership with elite assassination techniques.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance commanders consider VanCleef the premier internal security threat to southern human lands, paralyzing Westfall and the borders of Elwynn Forest."},kw={"brotherhood","deadmines","defias","moonbrook","stonemasons","stormwind","vancleef","westfall"},rel={"topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:stonemasons-guild","zone:deadmines","zone:westfall","npc:mathias-shaw","npc:baros-alexston","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","quest:373"},src={"Edwin VanCleef"}}
E["npc:gilnid"] = {t="npc",n="Gilnid",z="deadmines",s="Gilnid, known as the Smelter, is the goblin master engineer running the forges in the depths of the Deadmines. He oversees the smelting of raw ore into refined metal and munitions for Edwin VanCleef's hidden ironclad juggernaut. Without his fiery operations, the Defias Brotherhood would lack the heavy cannons needed to assault Stormwind.",h="Gilnid, known as the Smelter, is the goblin master engineer running the forges in the depths of the Deadmines.",sec={{t="Master of the Foundry",b="Deep within the Deadmines, the Defias Brotherhood relies on industrial expertise to forge weapons of war. Gilnid serves as VanCleef's head smelter, commanding a small army of goblin laborers, tinkers, and smiths in the central foundry. Towering over most of his kin, he drives his crew relentlessly through smoke and slag, barking orders and refusing breaks to ensure raw iron ore is processed into heavy plating and lethal ordnance.",sp=0},{t="Arming the Juggernaut",b="The smelting works are critical to the Brotherhood's grand ambition. Gilnid is directly responsible for forging the heavy cannons and ammunition intended for the colossal ironclad warship docked in the subterranean cove beyond his workshop. Until his foundry churns out every gun, barrel, and ball, the Defias vessel remains unready for its planned strike against Stormwind.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gilnid?",a="Gilnid is a goblin engineer and the head smelter for Edwin VanCleef in the Deadmines. He oversees the Brotherhood's forges and leads the industrial effort to cast cannons and ammunition for their war machine.",al={"gilnid deadmines","who is gilnid","the smelter"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Gilnid in the Deadmines?",a="The Defias Brotherhood hired mercenary goblin engineers to build and supply their hidden warship. Gilnid was placed in charge of the smelting works, transforming mined iron ore into refined parts, armor, and artillery.",al={"why is a goblin in deadmines","gilnid defias lore","what is gilnid doing"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Gilnid working on?",a="Gilnid is responsible for manufacturing the massive cannons, ship parts, and shot needed to arm the juggernaut hidden in the docks deeper inside the mines.",al={"gilnid cannon","what is gilnid building","deadmines forge purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why must Gilnid be defeated?",a="Gilnid controls the industrial foundry blocking the path to the cove. The heavy blast doors leading deeper toward the Defias ship remain sealed until the smelting room is secured.",al={"why kill gilnid","door past gilnid"},it="danger"},{q="Does Gilnid work directly for Edwin VanCleef?",a="Yes. He is not a member of the original Stonemasons, but rather a contracted goblin specialist serving directly under VanCleef to handle heavy metallurgy and weapons production.",al={"vancleef and gilnid","is gilnid defias leader"},it="ties"},{q="Why are there so many goblins around him?",a="Gilnid leads a specialized goblin engineering crew in the foundry. They operate the blast furnaces, pour molten iron, and assemble ordnance under his strict, unrelenting supervision.",al={"gilnid goblins","deadmines forge crew"},it="people"},{q="Whose side is Gilnid on?",a="Gilnid is firmly aligned with the Defias Brotherhood. While goblins are typically known for their independent mercenary contracts and neutrality, Gilnid has committed his formidable metallurgical talents to Edwin VanCleef's rebellious cause, serving as a chief overseer deep within the brotherhood's underground stronghold.",al={"gilnid faction","gilnid defias brotherhood","who does gilnid fight for"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Gilnid want?",a="Gilnid wants nothing more than to see the Defias juggernaut fully equipped and operational. As head smelter, his overriding drive is ensuring that every last cannon, casing, and round of heavy ammunition is forged to perfection, driving his goblin laborers mercilessly without rest until the massive warship is ready to sail.",al={"gilnid goal","what is gilnid trying to do","gilnid motivation"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The massive blast furnaces and smelting pots in Gilnid's workshop demonstrate how the Defias Brotherhood turns the raw mineral wealth of Westfall into refined iron and armaments.",["profession:Engineering"]="Gilnid's foundry is a prime example of goblin heavy industry, churning out standardized naval cannons, ammunition, and structural plating under extreme conditions.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stopping Gilnid shuts down the Defias weapons assembly line, preventing VanCleef's warship from being fully armed before it can threaten Stormwind Harbor."},kw={"cannons","deadmines","defias","forge","foundry","gilnid","goblin","juggernaut","smelter","vancleef"},rel={"npc:edwin-vancleef","zone:deadmines","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:goblin","quest:65"},src={"Gilnid"}}
E["npc:miner-johnson"] = {t="npc",n="Miner Johnson",z="deadmines",s="Miner Johnson is an elusive, seasoned miner affiliated with the Defias Brotherhood deep inside the Deadmines. Tucked away in a side alcove alongside ordinary laborers, this dangerous prospector oversees excavation efforts ahead of the heavy machinery found deeper underground. Because he wanders the subterranean tunnels erratically, adventurers only occasionally cross his path.",h="Miner Johnson is an elusive, seasoned miner affiliated with the Defias Brotherhood deep inside the Deadmines.",sec={{t="A Rare Face in the Deep",b="While hundreds of laborers pick at the subterranean veins of the Deadmines to supply Edwin VanCleef's hidden fortress, Miner Johnson stands out as an unusually formidable figure among them. Lurking in a shadowed alcove to the left before the lumbering shredders of the Mast Room, he is far tougher and more aggressive than the regular workforce. His unpredictable presence makes him a legendary target for explorers traversing the Defias tunnels.",sp=0},{t="Fueling the Defias War Machine",b="The Defias Brotherhood's clandestine operation beneath Moonbrook requires vast amounts of raw ore to forge weapons, reinforce shafts, and assemble mechanical contraptions. Miners like Johnson provide the muscle behind the metal, hacking away at the rich mineral seams beneath Westfall. Anyone stumbling into Johnson's workspace will quickly discover that he defends his dig site with lethal fervor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Miner Johnson?",a="Miner Johnson is a rare elite human miner allied with the Defias Brotherhood. He works deep within the Deadmines, situated in a side alcove with other laborers just before the goblin shredder.",al={"miner johnson lore","who is miner johnson","deadmines miner johnson"},it="identity"},{q="Where exactly is Miner Johnson located?",a="He can be found in the upper shafts of the Deadmines before reaching the room housing Sneed and his shredder. Look for a small excavation alcove off to the left where a pocket of miners are actively chipping away at the rock.",al={"miner johnson location","where is miner johnson","how to find miner johnson"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why isn't Miner Johnson always there?",a="Miner Johnson is a rare spawn, meaning he only appears occasionally when an expedition enters the Deadmines. Most groups running through the mine shafts will find an ordinary miner in his place instead.",al={"miner johnson not spawning","is miner johnson rare","miner johnson spawn rate"},gp=true},{q="Is Miner Johnson part of any quest?",a="Miner Johnson is not associated with any formal quest bounty. He is simply an opportunistic encounter for dungeon delve parties lucky enough to find him working the seam.",al={"miner johnson quest","does miner johnson have a quest"},gp=true},{q="What is Miner Johnson's role in the Deadmines?",a="He is an experienced foreman or master digger helping the Defias Brotherhood extract precious metal, stone, and resources necessary to construct their massive underground base and hidden juggernaut.",al={"what does miner johnson do","miner johnson role"},it="purpose"},{q="Is Miner Johnson dangerous compared to other miners?",a="Yes. While the standard diggers throughout the Deadmines are relatively fragile, Miner Johnson is an elite combatant with significantly more vitality and striking power, requiring a coordinated group to bring down safely.",al={"how hard is miner johnson","is miner johnson elite"},it="danger"},{q="Whose side is Miner Johnson on?",a="He stands with the Defias Brotherhood and their workforce. Toiling deep inside the Deadmines alongside the other laborers, Miner Johnson shares their allegiance to Edwin VanCleef's uprising, wielding his pick against any intruders who breach their subterranean stronghold.",al={"miner johnson faction","who does miner johnson work for","is miner johnson defias"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Miner Johnson in the Deadmines?",a="He is stationed in the alcoves above the foundry to dig out gold and iron for the Defias Brotherhood. While ordinary laborers keep the operation moving, Johnson oversees the pickaxes and helps supply the raw metal needed for Edwin VanCleef's secret projects.",al={"why is miner johnson here","miner johnson deadmines why","what brought miner johnson here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="For prospectors, Johnson represents the rugged, lawless side of subterranean labor, guarding rich mineral deposits deep beneath Westfall with blood and pickaxe.",["faction:Alliance"]="Striking down Johnson disrupts the steady stream of smeltable ore flowing into the Defias war machine hidden below Moonbrook."},kw={"alcove","deadmines","defias","elite","miner johnson","moonbrook","rare","shredder","westfall"},rel={"zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines"},src={"Miner Johnson"}}
E["npc:mr-smite"] = {t="npc",n="Mr. Smite",z="deadmines",s="Mr. Smite is the imposing tauren first mate serving aboard the Defias Brotherhood's flagship deep inside the Deadmines. An expert weaponmaster under Captain Greenskin, he commands the dockside approach to the hidden juggernaut with ruthless discipline. Intruders who face him must contend with his shifting arsenal and devastating physical strength.",h="Mr.",sec={{t="First Mate of the Cove",b="Guarding the docks of Ironclad Cove, Mr. Smite serves as first mate to the goblin Captain Greenskin. While the Defias Brotherhood is predominantly composed of disenfranchised humans and allied goblin tinkerers, Smite stands as a striking anomaly: a massive, battle-hardened tauren far from the plains of Kalimdor. Tasked with maintaining strict order among a rowdy pirate crew, he ensures that the labor fitting out Edwin VanCleef's secret dreadnaught proceeds without disruption.",sp=0},{t="A Deadly Weaponmaster",b="Smite is not merely a brute enforcer; he is a theatrical and versatile weaponmaster. He delights in toying with would-be heroes, deliberately prolonging combat to offer opponents a false sense of hope. When pressed, he unleashes a staggering, earth-shattering stomp that leaves foes stunned while he rummages through his nearby weapon chest. Beginning combat with a nimble dueling blade, he will escalate to twin cleaving reavers, and finally resort to his colossal two-handed warhammer when thoroughly provoked.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is a tauren working with human bandits in Westfall?",a="While the vast majority of tauren dwell in Kalimdor alongside their Horde allies, mercenary outcasts and wanderers occasionally find their way east. Smite serves as a pirate officer rather than an ideological follower of the Defias Brotherhood, hired alongside Captain Greenskin's crew to supervise the cove and ready the dreadnaught for sea.",al={"why tauren in deadmines","mr smite lore","tauren pirate"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Mr. Smite's superior?",a="Smite answers directly to Captain Greenskin, the goblin master of the pirate vessel anchored in Ironclad Cove. Above them both in the overall conspiracy stands Edwin VanCleef, the grand leader of the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"who is smite's boss","who does mr smite work for"},it="ties"},{q="What weapons does Mr. Smite use during the fight?",a="Smite begins battle with a Thief's Blade. As the fight turns against him, he retreats to his chest to equip a pair of Smite's Reavers, and finally draws out Smite's Mighty Hammer when pushed to his limits.",al={"smite weapons","what does smite pull out of the chest"},gp=true},{q="Where can Mr. Smite be found?",a="Mr. Smite stands watch on the wooden piers of Ironclad Cove, the final cavern within the Deadmines, guarding the gangplank leading up to the giant Defias dreadnaught.",al={"mr smite location","where is smite"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does Mr. Smite fight alone?",a="Smite keeps two stealthy Defias rogues hidden at his side, ready to ambush any trespassers who advance down the pier toward the ship.",al={"smite adds","smite bodyguards"},gp=true},{q="What makes Mr. Smite so dangerous in close quarters?",a="His signature tauren War Stomp sends shockwaves through the wooden dock, stunning entire parties of adventurers long enough for him to rearm himself from his footlocker and resume the assault with heavier weaponry.",al={"smite stun","smite war stomp"},it="danger"},{q="Who is Mr. Smite?",a="Mr. Smite is a formidable tauren weaponmaster serving as the first mate aboard the juggernaut hidden deep within the Deadmines. Working directly beneath Captain Greenskin, he commands the Defias Brotherhood's dock defenses and keeps their scoundrels in line with an iron fist and an arsenal of deadly weapons.",al={"who is smite","mr smite identity","what is mr smite"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Mr. Smite on?",a="Despite being a tauren, Mr. Smite owes no allegiance to the Horde or his kin in Kalimdor. He is firmly aligned with Edwin VanCleef's Defias Brotherhood, serving as second-in-command to their goblin naval commander, Captain Greenskin.",al={"mr smite faction","who does smite work for","is smite horde or defias"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Mr. Smite famous or feared?",a="Smite is feared for his sheer physical brutality and erratic combat mastery. He is notorious for toying with his victims, letting them believe they have gained the upper hand before stunning them with an earth-shattering stomp and drawing increasingly lethal weapons from his chest to finish them off.",al={"why is mr smite feared","mr smite reputation","why is smite famous"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Seeing a fellow tauren serving as a cutthroat first mate among seafaring outlaws in the Eastern Kingdoms is a jarring sight for any traveler from Mulgore.",["class:Warrior"]="Smite demonstrates remarkable martial discipline, seamlessly transitioning between swift single-handed strikes, dual-wielded axes, and punishing two-handed hammer blows.",["faction:Alliance"]="Smite serves as the primary barrier preventing Alliance agents from storming the gangplank to reach Captain Greenskin and Edwin VanCleef."},kw={"captain greenskin","deadmines","first mate","ironclad cove","mr smite","mr. smite","smite's mighty hammer","smite's reaver","tauren pirate","thief's blade"},rel={"subzone:ironclad-cove","npc:captain-greenskin","zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines","topic:tauren"},src={"Mr. Smite"}}
E["npc:rhahk-zor"] = {t="npc",n="Rhahk'Zor",z="deadmines",s="Rhahk'Zor is a hulking ogre serving as the head foreman within the Deadmines. Overseeing Edwin VanCleef's subterranean construction efforts, he keeps the Defias laborers and miners in line through sheer brute force and heavy-handed discipline.",h="Rhahk'Zor is a hulking ogre serving as the head foreman within the Deadmines.",sec={{t="The Foreman of the Deep",b="Deep beneath the rolling hills of Westfall, the Defias Brotherhood has transformed the abandoned gold mines of Moonbrook into an underground fortress. Coordinating this sprawling construction requires harsh discipline, a role filled by the ogre Rhahk'Zor. Appointed as head foreman, he oversees the excavation crews and laborers, driving them forward to carve out tunnels and assemble VanCleef's secret projects.",sp=0},{t="Brute Motivation",b="Rhahk'Zor maintains order through relentless muscle rather than careful engineering. Armed with an immense stone-headed hammer, his idea of workplace supervision is direct and unforgiving. Defias diggers and goblin engineers alike step lively around him, knowing that falling behind schedule or showing defiance invites a crushing blow from the towering taskmaster.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rhahk'Zor?",a="Rhahk'Zor is an ogre who acts as the primary foreman and enforcer for the Defias Brotherhood inside the Deadmines. He stands watch over the initial excavation tunnels, ensuring the workforce keeps digging without stepping out of line.",al={"rhahkzor","who is the ogre boss in deadmines","deadmines first boss"},it="identity"},{q="Why is an ogre working for the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Edwin VanCleef's rebellion relies on whatever muscle and mercenary talent they can acquire. An ogre provides unmatched physical intimidation, making Rhahk'Zor an ideal taskmaster to drive the grueling labor of excavating the mines.",al={"why is there an ogre in deadmines","rhahkzor defias"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Rhahk'Zor's job in the mines?",a="He serves as the head construction foreman. Rhahk'Zor supervises the miners, goblins, and Defias builders as they hollow out the caverns, maintain equipment, and build fortifications for the Brotherhood.",al={"what does rhahkzor do","rhahkzor role"},it="purpose"},{q="Where in the Deadmines is Rhahk'Zor located?",a="Rhahk'Zor guards the early quarry chambers of the Deadmines, standing past the initial miner tunnels and right before the heavy iron threshold known as Rhahk'Zor's Door.",al={"rhahkzor location","where is rhahkzor"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does Rhahk'Zor have any connection to the ogres from the First War?",a="Ogres once inhabited the Deadmines during the First War before being wiped out by Blackhand's Horde. Whether Rhahk'Zor is a lingering remnant of those earlier clans or simply a brute hired by VanCleef remains unconfirmed.",al={"first war ogres deadmines","ogre lore deadmines"},it="history"},{q="What happens when Rhahk'Zor is defeated?",a="Defeating Rhahk'Zor breaks the Defias hold on the outer quarry, clearing the way through the reinforced blast door he guards and allowing trespassers deeper into the clandestine shipyards and workshops.",al={"rhahkzor door","after rhahkzor"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Rhahk'Zor on?",a="Rhahk'Zor serves the Defias Brotherhood under Edwin VanCleef. Despite being an ogre among primarily human rogues and outlaws, he holds a position of authority as the head foreman overseeing the Brotherhood's subterranean excavation efforts and construction projects.",al={"who does rhahk'zor work for","rhahk'zor faction","rhahk'zor alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="Who is Rhahk'Zor tied to?",a="Rhahk'Zor answers directly to Edwin VanCleef, the mastermind behind the Defias Brotherhood. In turn, Rhahk'Zor commands the Defias miners, laborers, and guards stationed throughout the upper caverns of the Deadmines.",al={"rhahk'zor connections","who leads rhahk'zor","rhahk'zor edwin vancleef"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance adventurers pushing into Moonbrook, Rhahk'Zor is the first grim proof that the Defias Brotherhood has organized far beyond petty highway banditry into a heavily fortified army.",["class:Warrior"]="Facing Rhahk'Zor is a test of raw frontline endurance, pitted against a massive ogre swinging a sledgehammer that shatters stone and bone alike.",["profession:Mining"]="Rhahk'Zor drives his miners with crude brutality rather than respect for the veins of gold, churning Westfall's storied old mines into a rushed industrial war machine."},kw={"deadmines","defias","foreman","hammer","ogre","rhahk'zor","rhahkzor","vancleef"},rel={"zone:deadmines","topic:defias-brotherhood","npc:edwin-vancleef","subzone:deadmines","quest:65","topic:first-war"},src={"Rhahk'Zor"}}
E["npc:shoni-the-shilent"] = {t="npc",n="Shoni the Shilent",z="deadmines",s="Shoni the Shilent is an industrious gnome engineer stationed in Stormwind City's bustling Dwarven District. As commander of the Gnomeregan underground assault crew, she directs Alliance adventurers into the Deadmines to salvage the power supply of a goblin shredder, fuel for the machines she hopes will break a path back into Gnomeregan.",h="Shoni the Shilent is an industrious gnome engineer stationed in Stormwind City's bustling Dwarven District.",sec={{t="Commander of the Deep",b="Operating out of the smoky workshops of the Dwarven District, Shoni represents gnomish strategic ingenuity far from the lost halls of Gnomeregan. Her engineering plans are ambitious. With Gnomeregan in the hands of the troggs, Shoni is organizing an underground assault to retake it, and she sends operatives into the subterranean tunnels beneath Westfall for the parts her crew needs.",sp=0},{t="Subterranean Reclamation",b="Shoni's plan rests on the gnomes' own gyrodrillmatic excavationators, heavy drilling machines meant to break through the rocky underground borders of Gnomeregan and open the way for a gnomish assault. They lack the power to do it, so she wants the intact power supply, the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket, from a working goblin shredder deep in the Deadmines. Later, she also sends adventurers into Gnomeregan itself to tear apart its robots for spare parts to repair her fleet.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Shoni the Shilent?",a="Shoni the Shilent is a gnome quest giver located in Stormwind's Dwarven District. She acts as the commander of the Gnomeregan underground assault crew and coordinates subterranean reclamation missions.",al={"who is shoni","shoni lore","shoni the shilent npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Shoni?",a="She is stationed among the anvils and workshops of the Dwarven District in Stormwind City, near the blacksmithing and engineering areas.",al={"where is shoni","shoni location","find shoni"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Shoni interested in the Deadmines?",a="A functional goblin shredder works deep in the Deadmines. Shoni enlists adventurers to bring back its intact power supply, the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket, so her gyrodrillmatic excavationators can break through the underground borders of Gnomeregan.",al={"shoni deadmines","why send to deadmines","gyrodrillmatic quest"},it="wants"},{q="Why is she called 'the Shilent'?",a="The origin of Shoni's epithet is unknown. She is known for commanding the Gnomeregan underground assault crew.",al={"shoni nickname","why shilent","silent gnome"},it="name"},{q="Whose side is Shoni the Shilent on?",a="Shoni is loyal to Gnomeregan and the Grand Alliance. Operating out of the Dwarven District in Stormwind City, she serves as the commander of the Gnomeregan underground assault crew, coordinating specialized technical efforts on behalf of her displaced people.",al={"shoni faction","who does shoni work for","shoni the shilent alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Shoni the Shilent here in Stormwind?",a="Following the fall of Gnomeregan, Shoni established herself among the tinkerers and craftsmen of Stormwind's Dwarven District. From here, she directs the underground assault team and gathers the necessary mechanical components and weaponry needed to support ongoing gnome operations.",al={"why is shoni in stormwind","what is shoni doing here","shoni purpose"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Shoni the Shilent tied to?",a="Shoni commands the Gnomeregan underground assault crew, maintaining deep ties to the gnomish military and engineering ranks. Stationed within Stormwind City, she works in close coordination with fellow Alliance engineers and soldiers seeking to reclaim their technological heritage.",al={"shoni affiliations","who does shoni command","shoni allies"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For gnomish heroes, assisting Shoni brings their people one step closer to breaking back into Gnomeregan and reclaiming their fallen home.",["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers can appreciate the sheer mechanical complexity of the gyrodrillmatic excavationators Shoni hopes to power with a shredder's salvaged heart from beneath Moonbrook."},kw={"deadmines","dwarven district","excavationators","gnome","gyrodrillmatic","shilent","shoni","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:dwarven-district","zone:stormwind","zone:deadmines","quest:2040","quest:2928","quest:2041","topic:gnome","zone:gnomeregan"},src={"Shoni the Shilent"}}
E["npc:sneed"] = {t="npc",n="Sneed",z="deadmines",s="Sneed is the Defias Brotherhood's goblin lumbermaster stationed deep within the Deadmines. Operating from the lumber chamber known as the Mast Room, he pilots a heavy shredder of his own design to process timber for Edwin VanCleef's secret juggernaut.",h="Sneed is the Defias Brotherhood's goblin lumbermaster stationed deep within the Deadmines.",sec={{t="The Defias Lumbermaster",b="While the Defias Brotherhood draws its core membership from disenfranchised human stonemasons and common laborers, building an ironclad warship requires specialist trades. Edwin VanCleef recruited Sneed specifically for his engineering know-how and ruthless goblin efficiency. Stationed in the Mast Room along the subterranean rail network, Sneed oversees the rapid felling, cutting, and shaping of timber needed to frame VanCleef's colossal dreadnaught.",sp=0},{t="Industrial Brutality",b="Sneed's primary concern is cutting costs and meeting deadlined quotas, consequences be damned. To speed up the process, he commands the floor from inside a customized shredder equipped with oversized buzz saws. The deadly machine turns raw trunks into shipbuilding timber in seconds. If cornered by intruders, Sneed relies on the armor of his machine to grind them down, but he is more than willing to scramble out of the wreckage and fight with his bare hands if his contraption fails.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sneed?",a="Sneed is a goblin engineer and lumbermaster employed by Edwin VanCleef. He is tasked with overseeing the processing of lumber inside the Deadmines to build the Defias juggernaut.",al={"who is sneed","sneed lore","what is sneed"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Sneed be found?",a="Sneed is located in the Mast Room, an industrial lumber mill chamber situated along the mining tracks inside the Deadmines beneath Moonbrook.",al={"sneed location","where is sneed","sneed room"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is a goblin working for the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Edwin VanCleef needed specialized industrial knowledge and fast results to construct his secret warship. He hired mercenary goblins like Sneed who care little about politics or ethics as long as the coin is good.",al={"why is sneed with defias","goblin in deadmines","why defias hire goblins"},it="motive"},{q="What is Sneed piloting in battle?",a="Sneed pilots Sneed's Shredder, a heavy, saw-wielding bipedal mechanical harvester that he built himself to harvest and slice timber at terrifying speeds.",al={"sneed robot","sneed mech","sneed's shredder"},it="power"},{q="What happens when his shredder is destroyed?",a="Destroying the shredder does not finish the fight. Sneed ejects from the smoking remains of the machine and continues fighting intruders directly on foot.",al={"sneed phase 2","sneed out of shredder","does sneed die with shredder"},gp=true},{q="What is Sneed building timber for?",a="The timber cut in Sneed's chamber is transported downstream to the Ironclad Cove, where the Brotherhood is assembling a massive warship intended to strike back against Stormwind.",al={"why sneed cutting wood","mast room purpose","deadmines wood"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Sneed on?",a="Sneed works squarely for Edwin VanCleef and the Defias Brotherhood. While goblins are typically neutral merchants driven solely by profit, Sneed serves as VanCleef's dedicated lumbermaster. He oversees the Brotherhood's covert industrial logging deep within the Deadmines, throwing his engineering prowess and ruthless efficiency behind their campaign against Stormwind.",al={"sneed faction","who does sneed work for","is sneed defias"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Sneed want?",a="Sneed's goal is straightforward: build the Defias juggernaut as cheaply and swiftly as possible. Hired for his ruthless efficiency, he drives his logging operations around the clock, harvesting timber with his custom-built shredder to keep construction of the Brotherhood's secret warship moving without delay or costly waste.",al={"sneed goal","what is sneed trying to do","sneed motives"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Sneed here in the Deadmines?",a="Sneed is stationed in the Mast Room of the Deadmines to supply the heavy timber required for the Defias Brotherhood's massive naval vessel. Operating from the subterranean logging yard, he pilots his shredder to clear, mill, and prepare the massive wooden beams that will form the backbone of the juggernaut.",al={"why is sneed in deadmines","sneed purpose deadmines","why is sneed in the mast room"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Sneed tied to?",a="Sneed reports directly to Edwin VanCleef, the grand leader of the Defias Brotherhood. VanCleef contracted the goblin engineer to supervise lumber operations within the cavern system, integrating Sneed and his machinery into the broader Defias command hierarchy alongside figures like Rhahk'Zor and Gilnid.",al={"who does sneed report to","sneed edwin vancleef","sneed defias ties"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Sneed's customized shredder showcases classic goblin craftsmanship: devastatingly efficient, heavily armed, and pushed far past standard safety tolerances to maximize production speed.",["race:Gnome"]="Gnomish visitors to the Mast Room will find Sneed's machine a typical example of goblin ingenuity—loud, hazardous, and built without regard for operator comfort or structural longevity.",["faction:Alliance"]="Taking down Sneed cripples the supply of timber heading toward the Ironclad Cove, striking a critical blow against the Defias Brotherhood's shipbuilding efforts."},kw={"deadmines","edwin vancleef","goblin","juggernaut","lumbermaster","mast room","shredder","sneed","sneed's shredder"},rel={"npc:sneed-s-shredder","subzone:mast-room","zone:deadmines","npc:edwin-vancleef","topic:goblin"},src={"Sneed"}}
E["npc:sneed-s-shredder"] = {t="npc",n="Sneed's Shredder",z="deadmines",s="Sneed's Shredder is an imposing mechanised lumber harvester stationed deep within the Deadmines. Piloted by the goblin taskmaster Sneed, this deadly machine acts as both heavy industrial machinery for Edwin VanCleef's shipwrights and a terrifying perimeter defender.",h="Sneed's Shredder is an imposing mechanised lumber harvester stationed deep within the Deadmines.",sec={{t="Industrial Terror",b="Within the goblin-dominated foundry of the Deadmines, mechanical shredders serve a dual purpose: processing vast amounts of timber and lumber required for Edwin VanCleef's hidden juggernaut, and serving as armored shock engines against intruders. Sneed, the overseer of the lumber works, operates this modified mechanical beast directly, turning an oversized buzzsaw into an instrument of defense.",sp=0},{t="A Deadly Cockpit",b="Defeating the machine does not end the threat. Sneed perches inside an open cockpit above the spinning blades, relying on heavy iron plating and terrifying clatter to scatter his foes. Even when the machinery breaks down and the shredder collapses in a shower of sparks, Sneed leaps from the smoking wreckage to fight to the bitter end.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Sneed's Shredder used for in the Deadmines?",a="The Defias Brotherhood relies heavily on goblin machinery to carve through subterranean stone and process massive quantities of timber needed to construct their secret juggernaut. Sneed uses this shredder to mill wood and brutally enforce order over the underground works.",al={"why is there a shredder in deadmines","shredder purpose deadmines"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens when the shredder is destroyed?",a="When the shredder suffers critical mechanical failure, Sneed himself survives the wreckage. The goblin pilot emerges directly from the ruined vehicle, brandishing his own weapons and attacking intruders with fierce tenacity.",al={"does sneed die with the shredder","sneed shredder phase 2"}},{q="Why do the Defias Brotherhood have goblin technology?",a="Edwin VanCleef hired goblin engineers, craftsmen, and mercenary laborers to oversee the complex mechanical operations beneath Westfall, including steam-powered forges, gun foundries, and woodmills.",al={"defias goblins","why are goblins in deadmines"},it="ties"},{q="Can the shredder be hacked or controlled by engineers?",a="Clever inventors carrying a Gnomish Universal Remote can briefly override the shredder's control systems, temporarily wresting control of the machine away from Sneed.",al={"control sneed shredder","gnomish universal remote sneed"},gp=true},{q="Does Sneed's Shredder carry anything valuable?",a="Yes. Its intact power supply, the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket, is sought by Shoni the Shilent in Stormwind, who needs it to power the gnomes' gyrodrillmatic excavationators for an assault on Gnomeregan.",al={"sneed shredder quest item","what drops from sneed shredder"},gp=true},{q="Who pilots the shredder?",a="The machine is commanded by Sneed, a seasoned goblin supervisor who directs the logging and carpentry operations deep within the Deadmines.",al={"who drives sneed shredder","sneed pilot"},it="identity"},{q="Whose side is Sneed's Shredder on?",a="The mechanical beast fights under the banner of the Defias Brotherhood. While goblin engineers frequently work as neutral mercenaries for whoever pays best, Sneed and his armored timber-cutter are firmly committed to Edwin VanCleef's operation deep beneath Moonbrook.",al={"sneed shredder faction","who does sneed serve","is sneeds shredder defias"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Sneed want with his shredder?",a="Piloting a walking lumber mill bristling with spinning saw blades, Sneed is bent on reducing any intruders into fine planks of wood. Beyond processing timber and defending the subterranean works, he wants little more than to turn you into fresh sawdust for disturbing the Defias compound.",al={"sneed goals","what does sneed want","sneeds shredder purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Sneed's Shredder in the Deadmines?",a="Constructing an underground empire requires tremendous engineering support, lumber, and heavy defense. Sneed's Shredder is stationed in the lumber-filled caverns of the Deadmines to harvest timber for the Brotherhood's secret projects and to grind any trespassing Alliance agents into mulch.",al={"why is sneeds shredder here","why is sneed in deadmines","shredder location deadmines"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Why is Sneed's Shredder so feared?",a="Beyond its massive whirring sawblades, the mechanized terror strikes raw panic into the hearts of invaders. Sneed routinely unleashes frightful bursts of clattering noise and shrieking metal that terrify adventurers, sending them fleeing straight into the arms of waiting Defias goblins.",al={"why is sneeds shredder scary","sneeds shredder reputation","terrify sneeds shredder"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The shredder is a classic marvel of goblin mechanical design, though it remains vulnerable to the overrides of a Gnomish Universal Remote.",["race:Gnome"]="Shoni the Shilent of the Gnomeregan underground assault crew wants this goblin-built monster's power supply to drive the drills that could reopen the way to Gnomeregan.",["faction:Alliance"]="Eliminating Sneed and his machine cripples the lumber milling operations supporting Edwin VanCleef's secret war fleet."},kw={"buzzsaw","deadmines","defias","goblin","lumber","remote","shredder","sneed","vancleef"},rel={"npc:sneed","zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines","quest:2040","topic:goblin"},src={"Sneed's Shredder"}}
E["npc:wilder-thistlenettle"] = {t="npc",n="Wilder Thistlenettle",z="deadmines",s="Wilder Thistlenettle is a dwarven miner brooding in a tavern within Stormwind's Dwarven District. The sole survivor of a tragic cave-in deep within the Deadmines, he is haunted by the gruesome fate of his mining company and his brother.",h="Wilder Thistlenettle is a dwarven miner brooding in a tavern within Stormwind's Dwarven District.",sec={{t="A Bitter Survivor",b="Wilder Thistlenettle can be found drowning his sorrows in an alehouse near the southeastern gates of the Dwarven District. Years ago, he joined an expedition into the deep lodes of Moonbrook's Deadmines alongside his brother and their companions. A catastrophic cave-in sealed the rest of the crew in the dark while Wilder barely made it to the surface alive.",sp=0},{t="Ghosts of the Deep",b="The disaster in the tunnels did not end in peaceful rest. Wilder eventually learned that his brother and the lost mining company did not merely perish in the rubble—dark magic or unfinished business has animated them as restless undead, endlessly haunting the subterranean ruins. Consumed by grief and survivor's guilt, Wilder seeks brave adventurers willing to brave the Deadmines to recover mementos of the fallen and grant his brother final peace.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Wilder Thistlenettle?",a="He sits inside a quiet pub in Stormwind City's Dwarven District, located just inside the right side of the district's southeastern entrance.",al={"wilder thistlenettle location","where is wilder","thistlenettle stormwind"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happened to his brother in the Deadmines?",a="Wilder's brother was trapped in a sudden tunnel collapse alongside their fellow miners. Wilder escaped and seeks news of those left below.",al={"wilder brother deadmines","what happened to brother","thistlenettle brother lore"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Wilder need adventurers?",a="Wilder asks travelers heading into the Deadmines to recover personal mining union badges from the lost workers and investigate what happened to his brother.",al={"wilder quests","what does wilder want","collecting memories quest"},it="wants"},{q="Who is Wilder Thistlenettle?",a="Wilder Thistlenettle is a dwarven miner currently drinking his sorrows away in Stormwind City's Dwarven District. He was part of a mining expedition into the Deadmines alongside his brother, but tragedy struck deep beneath the earth.",al={"who is wilder","wilder thistlenettle lore","about wilder thistlenettle"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Wilder Thistlenettle on?",a="Wilder is loyal to the Alliance and his dwarven kin. He spends his days brooding in an empty tavern in Stormwind, seeking aid from trusted Alliance adventurers brave enough to enter the Deadmines.",al={"wilder thistlenettle faction","who does wilder work for","is wilder alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Wilder Thistlenettle here in Stormwind?",a="After narrowly escaping a catastrophic cave-in inside the Deadmines that claimed his brother and crew, Wilder fled back to the safety of Stormwind City. Traumatized and grief-stricken, he took refuge in a quiet tavern in the Dwarven District.",al={"why is wilder in stormwind","why is wilder here","wilder dwarven district why"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarven kin, Wilder's grief strikes a familiar cord, highlighting the ever-present perils of subterranean delvings and the sacred need to honor fallen guild brothers.",["profession:Mining"]="Miners readily understand the hazards of deep subterranean veins, where unstable earth and forgotten dark magic can entomb even seasoned crews."},kw={"brother","cave-in","deadmines","dwarven district","miner","stormwind","thistlenettle","wilder"},rel={"quest:167","quest:168","subzone:dwarven-district","zone:stormwind","zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines","topic:dwarf","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Wilder Thistlenettle"}}
E["quest:166"] = {t="quest",n="The Defias Brotherhood",z="deadmines",s="This mission represents the culmination of Gryan Stoutmantle's long campaign to reclaim Westfall from outlaw rule. Tasked with entering the Deadmines, Alliance champions must breach the criminal hideout and strike down the mastermind Edwin VanCleef himself.",h="This mission represents the culmination of Gryan Stoutmantle's long campaign to reclaim Westfall from outlaw...",sec={{t="A Sentence Passed",b="For months, Gryan Stoutmantle and the beleaguered People's Militia have fought a desperate holding action against the Defias Brotherhood across Westfall. With the true location of the thieves' stronghold uncovered beneath Moonbrook, Stoutmantle issues his final, grim decree: Edwin VanCleef must be assassinated to break the back of the rebellion once and for all.",sp=0},{t="Into the Labyrinth",b="To carry out the execution, fighters must delve deep into the winding shafts of the Deadmines. Past renegade stonemasons, goblin engineers, and heavy iron blast doors lies the central dry dock, where VanCleef oversees the final construction of his grand war vessel. Taking his head severs the command structure holding the entire outlaw network together.",sp=1},{t="Shadows of a Greater Conspiracy",b="While Stoutmantle believes VanCleef's death marks the beginning of the end for the Brotherhood, the fallen guildmaster's corpse holds troubling secrets. Upon his body rests an unsent letter, hinting that the uprising in Westfall was never an isolated revolt, but part of a wider, darker web stretching into the very nobility of Stormwind City.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the goal of this quest?",a="You are tasked by Gryan Stoutmantle to venture into the Deadmines dungeon in Moonbrook, eliminate Edwin VanCleef, and return with his severed head to Sentinel Hill.",al={"quest objective","what do i do","what is this quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who is Edwin VanCleef?",a="Edwin VanCleef was formerly the Grand Mason of the Stonemasons Guild who led the rebuilding of Stormwind City after the First and Second Wars. After a bitter dispute over payment with the House of Nobles, he founded the Defias Brotherhood to exact vengeance upon the kingdom.",al={"who is vancleef","vancleef identity","edwin vancleef lore"},it="target"},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle order an assassination?",a="The People's Militia lacks the regular army reinforcements from Stormwind needed to fight an enduring war. Stoutmantle recognizes that decapitating the leadership is Westfall's only realistic chance of breaking the syndicate's stranglehold on the farmlands.",al={"why kill vancleef","stoutmantle motive","why death penalty"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Edwin VanCleef be found?",a="He is hidden deep within the Deadmines beneath Moonbrook. Gryan Stoutmantle asks you to enter the hideout and seek him out.",al={"vancleef location","where is edwin vancleef","deadmines boss location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does killing VanCleef destroy the Defias completely?",a="Stoutmantle hopes VanCleef's death will break the Brotherhood's hold on Westfall. The outcome and any further discoveries await the assault.",al={"is defias defeated","are defias gone","end of brotherhood"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What item of note is found on VanCleef upon his defeat?",a="Stoutmantle demands VanCleef's head as proof. Other discoveries inside the hideout are revealed during the mission.",al={"vancleef drop","unsent letter","what does vancleef drop"},sp=1,it="item",gp=true},{q="What is the Head of VanCleef for?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle demands undeniable proof that Edwin VanCleef is truly dead. The Defias Brotherhood has terrorized Westfall from the shadows for years, spreading rumors and evading capture. Presenting VanCleef's severed head brings undeniable closure to the People's Militia and signals to the embattled farmers that their greatest tormentor has finally fallen.",al={"why take vancleefs head","head of vancleef purpose","why do i need vancleef head"},it="item",add=true},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle send you instead of the People's Militia?",a="The People's Militia is stretched to its limit simply defending Sentinel Hill and Westfall's scattered homesteads from daily bandit raids and gnoll incursions. Stormwind has refused to send reinforcements, leaving Stoutmantle without the disciplined, heavy strike force needed to breach the fortified depths of the Deadmines. He must rely on seasoned, capable adventurers like you to strike directly at the heart of the conspiracy.",al={"why doesn't the militia attack deadmines","why send me against vancleef","why doesn't stoutmantle kill vancleef"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of the kingdom, striking down VanCleef is a bittersweet tragedy, cutting down the very artisan whose hands rebuilt their capital out of ashes.",["faction:Alliance"]="This mission marks a critical early victory for the Alliance, securing the breadbasket of Westfall when the throne of Stormwind cannot spare its own troops.",["class:Rogue"]="VanCleef is a legendary rogue and master artisan; crossing blades with him in his inner sanctum tests the martial training of any stealth operative."},kw={"deadmines","head","juggernaut","militia","moonbrook","stonemasons","stoutmantle","vancleef","westfall"},rel={"npc:edwin-vancleef","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","zone:deadmines","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:westfall","quest:12","quest:65","topic:alliance"},m={start="Gryan Stoutmantle",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=166,ri={"Head of VanCleef"}},src={"The Defias Brotherhood (7)"}}
E["quest:167"] = {t="quest",n="Oh Brother. . .",z="deadmines",s="\"Oh Brother. . .\" is an Alliance mission given by Wilder Thistlenettle in Stormwind City. Distraught over a cave-in during an expedition into the depths beneath Moonbrook, Wilder asks adventurers to search the labyrinthine mines for his missing sibling, Foreman Thistlenettle, or recover his Explorers' League Badge.",h="\"Oh Brother.",sec={{t="A Trapped Expedition",b="Wilder Thistlenettle and his brother entered the cavernous subterranean tunnels beneath Moonbrook as members of a mining company. However, things turned catastrophic when hostile thieves swarmed the area and a violent cave-in sealed off the lower tunnels. Wilder managed to escape to Stormwind, but his brother and the rest of the crew were left trapped behind the rubble.",sp=0},{t="The Grim Fate of Foreman Thistlenettle",b="The truth awaiting any rescuer who pushes deep into the Deadmines tunnels is tragic. Foreman Thistlenettle did not survive the entombment; instead, dark energies stirring within the abandoned mines reanimated the unfortunate dwarf into an undead husk. Wandering the subterranean caverns alongside other restless corpses, the foreman retains only his prized Explorers' League Badge as a token of who he once was.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do I start the quest \"Oh Brother. . .\"?",a="The quest is offered by Wilder Thistlenettle, who can be found in the Dwarven District of Stormwind City.",al={"quest giver oh brother","who gives oh brother","where to get oh brother"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Where is Foreman Thistlenettle located?",a="Foreman Thistlenettle wanders the exterior mine corridors of the Deadmines, located beneath the town of Moonbrook in Westfall. He is in the undead-infested section of the tunnels outside the instance portal.",al={"foreman thistlenettle location","where is thistlenettle","where is the brother"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What happened to Foreman Thistlenettle?",a="A cave-in trapped Foreman Thistlenettle and his mining party inside the caverns, and none of them have been heard from since. Finding him, or at least his badge, is the only way Wilder will learn his brother's fate.",al={"is thistlenettle alive","what happened to the brother","thistlenettle lore"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="What item do I need to retrieve?",a="You need to retrieve Foreman Thistlenettle's Explorers' League Badge, which he always carried; find the foreman deep in the Deadmines tunnels and the badge will be with him.",al={"oh brother quest item","what drops for oh brother"},sp=1,it="item",gp=true},{q="What was the expedition doing in Moonbrook?",a="The Thistlenettle brothers were members of a mining company working the vast mine beneath Moonbrook before being ambushed by Defias bandits and separated by a sudden tunnel collapse.",al={"why were the dwarves in westfall","explorers league deadmines","why were they in moonbrook"},it="history"},{q="Is this quest completed inside the Deadmines dungeon instance?",a="No, you do not need to zone inside the dungeon instance. Foreman Thistlenettle is an elite mob who roams the contested mine tunnels that lead up to the instance portal.",al={"is oh brother inside deadmines instance","do i need a dungeon group"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Wilder Thistlenettle want this done?",a="Wilder barely escaped with his life when the tunnels collapsed deep beneath Moonbrook. His brother and the rest of the mining expedition never emerged, swallowed by the dark and the thieves infesting the passages. Left in agonizing uncertainty back in Stormwind, Wilder seeks peace of mind. He needs to know whether his brother yet lives or if he met a grim fate in the deep.",al={"why does wilder want his brother found","wilder thistlenettle motive","why find foreman thistlenettle"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is Thistlenettle's Badge?",a="Foreman Thistlenettle carried an Explorers' League Badge marking his standing with Ironforge's guild of diggers and adventurers. Should you find no living dwarf in the depths, recovering this personal token serves as proof of his fate, granting his grieving brother final closure.",al={"what is thistlenettles badge","thistlenettle explorers league badge","why get the badge"},it="item",add=true},{q="Why does Wilder Thistlenettle ask you instead of going himself?",a="Wilder barely made it out alive when disaster struck. The sprawling labyrinth beneath Moonbrook is crawling with cutthroats and dangerous hazards, far beyond what an escaped miner can brave alone. Seeing a capable adventurer, he places his hopes on you to succeed where he could only flee.",al={"why doesnt wilder go himself","why send me deadmines","why does wilder need help"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The tragic demise of an Explorers' League foreman in human lands hits home for any dwarf who values brotherhood, stonecutting, and the League's tireless work.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Deadmines are a blight on Stormwind's doorstep, and this quest shows how deeply the Defias and subterranean horrors have harmed innocent citizens."},kw={"badge","deadmines","explorers' league","moonbrook","stormwind","thistlenettle","undead","westfall","wilder"},rel={"npc:wilder-thistlenettle","zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines","subzone:moonbrook","zone:westfall","topic:explorers-league","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Wilder Thistlenettle",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=167,ri={"Thistlenettle's Badge"}},src={"Oh Brother. . ."}}
E["quest:168"] = {t="quest",n="Collecting Memories",z="deadmines",s="Collecting Memories is a solemn task entrusted by the dwarven miner Wilder Thistlenettle in Stormwind City. He asks adventurers braving the ruined mines beneath Moonbrook to recover the Miners' Union Cards of his fallen coworkers. Bringing these tokens back offers grieving families in the capital closure following a catastrophic cave-in.",h="Collecting Memories is a solemn task entrusted by the dwarven miner Wilder Thistlenettle in Stormwind City.",sec={{t="A Tragic Collapse",b="Before Moonbrook fell completely into lawlessness and the shadow of the Defias Brotherhood, the mines of Westfall were an active source of livelihood for many working-class families. Wilder Thistlenettle survived a devastating cave-in that buried a wing of the labyrinthine tunnels, but many of his friends and coworkers were not so fortunate. Cut off from rescue, those workers perished deep underground, leaving behind mourning kin in Stormwind who never received true confirmation or closure regarding their loved ones' fates.",sp=0},{t="Restless Remains",b="The tunnels outside the main subterranean iron works are no longer silent tombs. The souls of the miners who perished in the collapse now wander the dark passages as restless, undead husks. To recover the Miners' Union Cards, travelers must navigate these haunted shafts, facing the animated remains of the very diggers Wilder once worked alongside. Returning these cards to Stormwind ensures their kin finally learn the truth and gives Wilder a chance to honor his fallen brethren.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Wilder Thistlenettle?",a="Wilder Thistlenettle is a dwarven miner residing in Stormwind City. Having survived a catastrophic tunnel cave-in beneath Westfall that claimed the lives of his close coworkers, he seeks to bring peace and confirmation to their surviving families.",al={"wilder thistlenettle","quest giver","who gives collecting memories"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to the miners in the Deadmines?",a="A devastating tunnel collapse trapped and killed an entire crew of miners in a wing of the Moonbrook dig sites. Deprived of rescue and proper burial, their spirits and bodies have risen as restless undead haunting the abandoned passages.",al={"why are there undead miners","mine collapse","deadmines cave in"},it="history"},{q="Why does Wilder want their Miners' Union Cards?",a="The union cards serve as formal identification for the workers who died in the collapse. Because the bodies were never recovered, retrieving their cards allows Wilder to formally notify their families in Stormwind and offer them closure.",al={"what are the union cards for","miners union cards"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the union cards found?",a="The cards are found in the haunted, outer tunnels beneath Moonbrook, situated in the corridors just before entering the secured threshold of the Deadmines proper.",al={"where do i find the cards","undead deadmines location","where are the dead miners"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Did the Defias Brotherhood cause the cave-in?",a="Wilder Thistlenettle simply recalls it as a horrible mining accident and tunnel cave-in. While the Defias Brotherhood now rules the deep passages of the Deadmines, the tragedy itself appears to be a disastrous industrial collapse that trapped his fellow miners.",al={"did defias cause the cave in","who collapsed the mine"},it="conflict"},{q="Are the miners considered part of the Defias Brotherhood?",a="No. They were ordinary union laborers working the mines when the cave-in struck. Their restless undead remnants roam the cavern peripheries separate from Edwin VanCleef's organized Defias forces further inside.",al={"are dead miners defias","are undead miners with defias"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Miners' Union Card?",a="These union cards served as official identification for the laborers working the rich veins of the Moonbrook mines before the catastrophe. Now, they are the only lasting proof of who perished beneath the earth when the tunnels collapsed. Recovering them is the sole way to confirm which specific workers met their end in the depths, allowing Wilder Thistlenettle to notify their grieving families in Stormwind and offer them closure.",al={"miners union card","what are the union cards","union card"},it="item",add=true},{q="Why does Wilder Thistlenettle need an adventurer for this task?",a="Wilder Thistlenettle survived the terrible collapse, but the depths of the Moonbrook mines have since fallen into perilous chaos. The area surrounding the old cave-in is overrun with hostile forces and restless dead, far beyond what an ordinary civilian or former miner can face. Without official city guards dispatched into the treacherous ruins of Westfall, Wilder relies on capable adventurers who already intend to delve into the mines to search the wreckage for his lost friends.",al={"why me collecting memories","why does wilder need help","why send an adventurer"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Every miner understands the lingering dread of a shaft collapse, giving this mission to recover lost union cards a profound, somber resonance for pick-wielders.",["race:Dwarf"]="Dwarves place great value on the bonds forged underground and the sanctity of fallen brethren, making Wilder Thistlenettle's plea personal to fellow stone-kin.",["faction:Alliance"]="Retrieving the tokens of fallen Westfall workers directly supports the grieving working-class families enduring hard times within the walls of Stormwind."},kw={"collecting memories","deadmines","miners union card","moonbrook","stormwind","undead miners","wilder thistlenettle"},rel={"npc:wilder-thistlenettle","zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines","subzone:moonbrook","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Wilder Thistlenettle",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=168,ri={"Miners' Union Card"}},src={"Collecting Memories"}}
E["quest:2040"] = {t="quest",n="Underground Assault",z="deadmines",s="Underground Assault is an Alliance quest offered by Shoni the Shilent in Stormwind City's Dwarven District. Tasked with aiding the displaced gnomes, adventurers venture into the Deadmines to salvage an intact power core from a goblin shredder. This stolen component is destined to power drilling machines intended to spearhead the liberation of Gnomeregan.",h="Underground Assault is an Alliance quest offered by Shoni the Shilent in Stormwind City's Dwarven District.",sec={{t="A Desperate Ingenuity",b="Following the catastrophic fall of Gnomeregan to the primitive troggs, surviving gnomish tinkerers have been forced into exile across Khaz Modan and Stormwind. Rather than wallowing in defeat, engineers like Shoni the Shilent are already devising mechanical operations to breach their lost home. The primary obstacle is the dense, subterranean rock surrounding the technocratic city, requiring massive tunneling engines known as gyrodrillmatic excavationators. Lacking the necessary localized power grids in human lands, the gnomes have turned their sights to an unlikely and volatile alternative: goblin heavy machinery operating in the criminal underworld.",sp=0},{t="Looting the Defias Foundries",b="Deep within the twisting shafts of the Deadmines in Westfall, Edwin VanCleef's Defias Brotherhood employs goblin engineers to manufacture war machines, including a fully operational goblin shredder. Shoni directs Alliance operatives to infiltrate this foundry, destroy or dismantle the lumbering automaton, and recover its specialized heart—the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket. By commandeering the potent goblin power supply, the exiled gnomes gain the raw mechanical output needed to bore through the subterranean perimeter and launch a counteroffensive to reclaim Gnomeregan.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the Underground Assault quest?",a="The quest is given by Shoni the Shilent, a gnomish engineer located in the Dwarven District of Stormwind City. Adventurers are often directed to her after speaking with other gnomes who mention her ambitious plans.",al={"quest giver underground assault","who gives underground assault","shoni quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I find the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket?",a="The Gnoam Sprecklesprocket is recovered from a functional goblin shredder deep within the foundry tunnels of the Deadmines in Westfall.",al={"sprecklesprocket location","where is sprecklesprocket","shredder part deadmines"},gp=true},{q="Why does Shoni need parts from a goblin shredder?",a="Gnomish gyrodrillmatic excavationators need an immense, portable power supply to breach the reinforced subterranean borders around Gnomeregan. The heavy-duty power core running the Defias Brotherhood's goblin shredder provides the exact mechanical output required for the drills.",al={"why goblin parts","why shredder power supply","sprecklesprocket purpose"},it="motive"},{q="What is the broader goal of this mission?",a="The mission supports the future liberation of Gnomeregan. By powering up heavy excavation drills, the exiled gnomes intend to tunnel directly through the rocky perimeter of their captured city and mount a surprise assault against the occupying troggs.",al={"why do underground assault","reclaiming gnomeregan quest","gnome assault plan"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened to Gnomeregan that caused this assault to be planned?",a="Gnomeregan was overwhelmed by a subterranean trogg invasion emerging from deep beneath the city. In the chaotic defense, the city was contaminated by toxic radiation, forcing the surviving gnomish populace to flee to Ironforge and Stormwind as refugees.",al={"why did gnomeregan fall","what happened to gnomeregan","trogg invasion"},it="history"},{q="Are the Defias Brotherhood and the troggs allied?",a="No, they have no connection. The Defias Brotherhood merely hired goblin tinkerers to build warmachines in Westfall. Shoni simply exploits the Defias presence in the Deadmines as a convenient source of high-yield goblin technology.",al={"defias and troggs","are troggs with defias"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket?",a="The Gnoam Sprecklesprocket is an intact, highly efficient goblin power supply housed within the shredder operating deep inside the Deadmines. Shoni the Shilent intends to integrate this power core directly into gnomish gyrodrillmatic excavationators. These heavy drilling machines need immense energy to bore through the dense, rocky underground perimeter shielding Gnomeregan, carving an entryway for the gnomish assault forces waiting to reclaim their home.",al={"what is gnoam sprecklesprocket","sprecklesprocket purpose","what does the shredder power supply do"},it="item",add=true},{q="Why does Shoni send you after the goblin shredder in the Deadmines?",a="The Defias Brotherhood employs advanced goblin engineering, including a fully functional timber and mining shredder, to excavate and construct their secret operations beneath Moonbrook. Because these war machines utilize remarkably potent power cores, Shoni identified this machine as a prime salvage target. You are sent to dismantle or destroy the shredder deep inside the compound and extract its intact power unit before the Brotherhood puts it to further use.",al={"who is the target in deadmines","why kill the shredder","why is there a shredder in deadmines"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For exiled gnomish adventurers, salvaging this power core is a personal step toward piercing the rocky walls of their fallen home and driving the troggs out of Gnomeregan.",["profession:Engineering"]="Tinkers will appreciate the audacious engineering behind cannibalizing a brutal goblin shredder power core to fuel precision gnomish excavation machinery.",["faction:Alliance"]="Assisting the displaced gnomes of the Dwarven District strengthens the bond between Stormwind and its exiled allies while striking a blow against the Defias supply line."},kw={"deadmines","gnoam sprecklesprocket","gnomeregan","goblin shredder","gyrodrillmatic","shoni the shilent","troggs","underground assault"},rel={"npc:shoni-the-shilent","quest:2041","zone:deadmines","zone:gnomeregan","topic:gnome","topic:goblin","topic:trogg","quest:2928"},m={start="Shoni the Shilent",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=2040,ri={"Gnoam Sprecklesprocket"}},src={"Underground Assault"}}
E["quest:214"] = {t="quest",n="Red Silk Bandanas",z="deadmines",s="Red Silk Bandanas is a mission issued by Scout Riell on behalf of the People's Militia. It directs Alliance adventurers into the Deadmines to hunt down high-ranking Defias operatives and bring back their distinctive red silk masks as proof.",h="Red Silk Bandanas is a mission issued by Scout Riell on behalf of the People's Militia.",sec={{t="A Hierarchy in Cloth",b="While common cutpurses and highwaymen throughout Westfall tie coarse red cloth around their faces, the Defias Brotherhood maintains a strict internal hierarchy indicated by fabric. Scout Riell and the People's Militia have discovered that rank-and-file bandits wear rough weave, while senior conspirators and inner-circle operatives are distinguished by fine red silk. Stripping these bandanas directly targets the experienced officers coordinating Edwin VanCleef's uprising.",sp=0},{t="Striking the Core",b="Because silk marks seniority, the greatest concentration of these high-ranking outlaws gathers deep within the Deadmines beneath Moonbrook. Sentinels and scouts stationed outside Sentinel Hill rely on freelance champions to push into the contested subterranean tunnels. Every silk bandana recovered represents one less lieutenant organizing ambushes, defending weapon caches, or enforcing VanCleef's rule across Westfall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do the Defias wear red bandanas?",a="The red bandana serves as the unified emblem and calling card of the Defias Brotherhood across Stormwind's territories. It conceals their identities while signaling allegiance to Edwin VanCleef's rebellious movement.",al={"defias mask meaning","why red masks","defias uniform"},it="item"},{q="What makes the red silk bandanas special compared to regular bandanas?",a="According to Scout Riell, the fabric denotes status within the Brotherhood. Common street thugs wear coarse, cheap material, while veterans, officers, and trusted lieutenants are awarded red silk.",al={"why red silk","silk vs cloth defias","silk bandana difference"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Scout Riell?",a="Scout Riell is an operative serving the People's Militia in Westfall, tasked with tracking Defias movements and directing adventurers to strike at their strongholds around the Deadmines.",al={"scout riell westfall","who gives red silk bandanas quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the Defias wearing silk bandanas located?",a="They are concentrated in and around the Deadmines beneath the town of Moonbrook, where Edwin VanCleef's senior forces oversee underground operations.",al={"where to find silk bandanas","deadmines silk bandana location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the People's Militia?",a="The People's Militia is a volunteer defense force formed by Gryan Stoutmantle and the embattled farmers of Westfall to protect their lands after the Stormwind army failed to provide adequate garrisons.",al={"who are the people's militia","peoples militia westfall"},it="allies"},{q="Do these bandanas have any use outside of proving a kill?",a="For the People's Militia, they serve purely as indisputable proof that high-ranking outlaws have been eliminated, weakening the command structure of the Brotherhood.",al={"can you wear red silk bandana","what are the bandanas for"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why does Scout Riell want Defias bandanas collected?",a="Scout Riell is seeking to strike a decisive blow against the leadership of the Defias Brotherhood on behalf of the People's Militia. The militia knows that silk bandanas denote high-ranking officers rather than mere thugs. By eliminating these key figures and demanding their bandanas as proof, Riell hopes to shatter the brotherhood's command structure and finally reclaim Westfall for its people.",al={"why scout riell bandanas","scout riell motive","why collect red silk bandanas"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who are you being sent against?",a="You are hunting the elite officers and veterans of the Defias Brotherhood stationed in and around Edwin VanCleef's stronghold within the Deadmines. Unlike the rough cutthroats roaming Westfall's farmsteads, these high-ranking members guard the brotherhood's base of operations, oversee the hidden works deep beneath Moonbrook, and direct the syndicate's operations across the region.",al={"who are we hunting","red silk bandana target","who drops silk bandanas"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why does Scout Riell ask you instead of the Stormwind guards?",a="Stormwind has virtually abandoned Westfall, offering little to no military support while the House of Nobles ignores the growing crisis. The local People's Militia is stretched thin, lacking the numbers, training, and resources to mount a frontal assault against fortified criminal bastions. Riell and her fellow scouts must rely on capable adventurers to infiltrate the treacherous Deadmines and confront the brotherhood's leadership directly.",al={"why not stormwind army","why send an adventurer","why need me"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Every officer felled in the Deadmines loosens the Brotherhood's stranglehold on the breadbasket of the Kingdom of Stormwind.",["class:Rogue"]="The Defias's red silk masks represent a notorious tradition of underworld tradecraft, marking veteran cutthroats and covert conspirators.",["profession:Tailoring"]="Fine red silk is an expensive luxury for common bandits, underscoring how lavishly equipped and funded the Brotherhood's leadership truly is."},kw={"deadmines","defias brotherhood","moonbrook","peoples militia","red silk bandanas","scout riell","vancleef","westfall"},rel={"npc:scout-riell","zone:deadmines","quest:12","subzone:deadmines"},m={start="Scout Riell",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=214},src={"Red Silk Bandanas"}}
E["subzone:goblin-foundry"] = {t="subzone",n="Goblin Foundry",z="deadmines",s="The Goblin Foundry is an industrial workshop deep within the Deadmines where goblin tinkerers manufacture heavy metalwork for the Defias Brotherhood. A massive smelting cauldron dominates the chamber, which remains occupied by goblin craftsmen and engineers under Gilnid.",h="The Goblin Foundry is an industrial workshop deep within the Deadmines where goblin tinkerers manufacture...",sec={{t="Industrial Ambitions",b="Carved into the subterranean depths of Moonbrook, the Goblin Foundry provides the Defias Brotherhood with heavy manufacturing power. Goblin craftsmen and engineers work among the smelters and iron ramps, producing anchors and cannonballs.",sp=0},{t="Gilnid's Workshop",b="Gilnid presides over the foundry's goblin workforce. Craftsmen maintain production while engineers defend the workshop with remote-controlled golems, making its narrow ramps and molten metal dangerous for intruders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was being built in the Goblin Foundry?",a="The goblin craftsmen produce heavy metalwork, including anchors and cannonballs, for the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"what are they making here","foundry purpose","deadmines factory"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are there golems in the foundry?",a="Goblin engineers use remote-controlled golems to defend their workshop against intruders.",al={"why golems here","foundry robots","mechanical enemies deadmines"},it="threat"},{q="Where are the goblins who ran this workshop?",a="The goblin craftsmen and engineers remain at work in the foundry under Gilnid, the smelter.",al={"where are the goblins","foundry engineers","gilnid workers"},it="residents"},{q="What is the large structure in the center of the room?",a="The center of the room is dominated by a massive industrial smelting cauldron used to melt down ore hauled from the mines to forge armor plates and mechanical chassis.",al={"foundry center pot","smelting vat","cauldron in deadmines"}},{q="What is the Goblin Foundry?",a="The Goblin Foundry is a cavernous industrial workshop nestled deep within the Deadmines subterranean complex. Built and operated by mercenary goblin engineers contracted to the Defias Brotherhood, the facility houses massive smelting equipment, catwalks, and workshops intended to forge metalworks, tools, and mechanized implements of war for Edwin VanCleef's hidden rebellion.",al={"what is goblin foundry","goblin foundry lore","what is this foundry"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at the Goblin Foundry?",a="Goblin craftsmen and engineers established the foundry as an active Defias workshop. Gilnid directs their metalworking, while engineers employ remote-controlled golems to defend it.",al={"what happened here","foundry history","goblin foundry story"},it="history",add=true},{q="What work is done at the Goblin Foundry?",a="The foundry remains active. Goblin craftsmen and engineers work there under Gilnid, producing metalwork for the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"what work is done at goblin foundry","what do goblins make at the foundry","goblin foundry production"},it="purpose",add=true},{q="Is the Goblin Foundry dangerous?",a="The foundry is dangerous to intruders. Goblin craftsmen, engineers, and their remote-controlled golems defend narrow ramps around a massive smelting cauldron.",al={"is goblin foundry dangerous","foundry dangers","goblin foundry threat"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Goblin Foundry?",a="The chamber is named after the goblin tinkerers and metallurgists hired by the Defias Brotherhood to run it. It was tailored specifically for goblin engineering and smelting, complete with elaborate ramps, blast cauldrons, and workbenches designed around their explosive industrial ambitions.",al={"why is it called goblin foundry","goblin foundry name origin","who named goblin foundry"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The foundry showcases goblin metalworking and mechanical ingenuity, with engineers using remote-controlled golems to defend the workshop.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Defias workshop reveals the scale of the Brotherhood's industrial resources beneath Westfall."},kw={"cauldron","deadmines","defias","goblin foundry","vancleef"},rel={"zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines","subzone:cauldron","topic:goblin"},src={"Goblin Foundry"}}
E["subzone:ironclad-cove"] = {t="subzone",n="Ironclad Cove",z="deadmines",s="Ironclad Cove is a massive subterranean cavern hidden beneath Westfall, housing an underground shipyard and dock. It serves as the secret construction dock for the Defias Brotherhood's war juggernaught and connects directly to the sea.",h="Ironclad Cove is a massive subterranean cavern hidden beneath Westfall, housing an underground shipyard and...",sec={{t="The Hidden Shipyard",b="Buried at the deepest point of the Deadmines, Ironclad Cove is a monumental sea cavern converted into a fortified dockyard. Here, Edwin VanCleef and the Defias Brotherhood have constructed an enormous warship known as the juggernaught. The cavern features extensive wooden scaffolding, islets, and loading catwalks manned by Defias pirates, deckhands, and overseers. Its existence reveals the true scale of the Defias threat: VanCleef intends not merely to raid Westfall's farmsteads, but to assemble a private naval force capable of bombarding the shores of Stormwind itself.",sp=0},{t="Gateway to the Ocean",b="The cavern is dominated by colossal iron-reinforced sea doors set into the rock wall. Once opened, these gates provide a direct outlet into the Great Sea, emerging along the coastline just north of Stranglethorn Vale. Before the Defias Brotherhood seized the cove, it was held by an independent pirate crew whom the Brotherhood slaughtered to ensure total secrecy. Shielded from the eyes of the Stormwind naval fleet, the cove provides the Brotherhood an unmonitored lane for moving contraband, staging maritime raids, and preparing their naval assault.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the ship in Ironclad Cove being built for?",a="The juggernaught is the centerpiece of Edwin VanCleef's military ambitions. The Defias Brotherhood assembled this massive warship deep beneath the earth so it could launch undetected through subterranean water channels and strike at Stormwind from the sea.",al={"why is there a ship here","what is the juggernaught","deadmines ship purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does the large metal door in the cove lead?",a="The massive gates open directly into the ocean along the southern coast of Westfall, near the border of northern Stranglethorn Vale. When opened, the juggernaught can sail straight out into the Great Sea.",al={"where do the sea gates open","deadmines iron doors","exit into the ocean"},it="place"},{q="Who controls Ironclad Cove?",a="The Defias Brotherhood holds the cove under the command of Edwin VanCleef. While independent pirates originally used the secluded cavern, VanCleef's forces wiped them out to commandeer the docks and keep the juggernaught's construction entirely secret.",al={"who runs the cove","who lives in ironclad cove"},it="residents"},{q="Who is the murloc aboard the ship?",a="That is Cookie, the Defias ship's cook. Armed with a rolling pin and cooking cauldrons, he is an unusual ally among the human and goblin renegades, having claimed the galley as his personal domain.",al={"cookie the murloc","why is there a murloc pirate","chef cookie"}},{q="What is Ironclad Cove?",a="Ironclad Cove is a vast subterranean cavern deep beneath the Deadmines, transformed into a secret shipyard. Enclosed by towering stone walls and natural waterways, it houses the docks and scaffolding where the Defias Brotherhood constructs their massive war juggernaut. A colossal reinforced door seals the cavern off from the southern seas, concealing their naval operation from the Kingdom of Stormwind until the ship is fully prepared to sail.",al={"ironclad cove info","what is this place deadmines","deadmines ship cavern"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Ironclad Cove?",a="Before the Defias Brotherhood took control, Ironclad Cove was held by an independent pirate crew. When Edwin VanCleef and his conspirators laid claim to the Deadmines, the Defias ruthlessly slaughtered the resident pirates to secure the cavern for their own clandestine shipbuilding. Later, Jerias Bloodvein and his Bloodsail Buccaneers attempted to invade the hideout, though the Defias firmly retained their grip over the docks.",al={"ironclad cove history","who had ironclad cove before","deadmines shipyard past"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is Ironclad Cove dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. Ironclad Cove serves as the inner redoubt and nerve center of Edwin VanCleef's rebellion. The waters, catwalks, and scaffolding swarming with heavily armed Defias cutpurses, hired corsairs, goblin engineers, and deadly combatants defending their prized warship. Anyone who infiltrates this deep into the mine complex faces the most formidable commanders of the Brotherhood, determined to protect their master plan at all costs.",al={"is ironclad cove safe","ironclad cove threats","deadmines shipyard danger"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Finding a full-sized war galleon buried under Westfall transforms the Defias from a regional bandit gang into an existential military threat against the Kingdom of Stormwind.",["class:Rogue"]="The cove represents the zenith of Edwin VanCleef's craftsmanship, engineering prowess, and underground logistics, making it legendary among thieves and outlaws."},kw={"cookie","deadmines ship","defias cove","edwin vancleef","ironclad cove","juggernaught","shipyard"},rel={"zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines","npc:cookie","topic:pirate","zone:stranglethorn"},src={"Ironclad Cove"}}
E["subzone:mast-room"] = {t="subzone",n="Mast Room",z="deadmines",s="The Mast Room is a cavernous subterranean lumber mill nestled deep within the Deadmines. Overseen by the goblin taskmaster Sneed and his woodcarvers, this chamber processes timber stripped from Westfall.",h="The Mast Room is a cavernous subterranean lumber mill nestled deep within the Deadmines.",sec={{t="The Underground Sawmill",b="Past the deeper mine tunnels of the Deadmines lies the Mast Room, a massive cavern converted into a fully functional lumber mill. Piles of felled timber, sawdust, and massive cutting equipment dominate the space. It is here that goblin woodcarvers shape the immense masts, ribs, and planks needed to assemble the massive warship hidden further within the Ironclad Cove. Under the watchful eye of Sneed, the Defias Brotherhood transforms Westfall's harvested wood into instruments of war.",sp=1},{t="Industrial Labor",b="The chamber is an example of goblin industry at its most relentless. Sneed oversees operations from atop a mechanical shredder, ensuring the woodcarvers maintain grueling quotas. Massive logs are hoisted and planed in constant succession, turning what was once a dormant gold mine into a roaring, soot-choked naval shipyard.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is there a lumber mill inside an underground mine?",a="The Defias Brotherhood is secretly building a massive warship inside the cove beneath the mines. The Mast Room serves as the assembly and shaping ground for the ship's masts, framing, and hull planks, using timber smuggled from the surface of Westfall.",al={"why timber here","why wood in deadmines","mast room purpose"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Who runs the Mast Room?",a="The chamber is overseen by Sneed, a goblin master craftsman who directs the goblin woodcarvers while piloting a lethal mechanical lumber shredder.",al={"mast room boss","who leads mast room","who is sneed"},it="residents"},{q="Why are goblins working here for the Defias?",a="Edwin VanCleef hired goblin engineers and craftsmen to provide technical expertise that human stonemasons lacked. The goblins provide heavy machinery, explosives, and shipwright skills in exchange for gold and profit.",al={"why are goblins in deadmines","defias goblins"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="What is the Mast Room?",a="The Mast Room is an underground lumber mill and woodworking chamber tucked deep within the Deadmines, located just past the secondary mine shafts. Operated by hired goblin craftsmen, it is dedicated to shaping timber into critical components—most notably the heavy masts and structural woodwork—needed for Edwin VanCleef's secret juggernaut docked further in the cavern.",al={"what is mast room","mast room deadmines","about mast room"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Mast Room?",a="It earned its name from its primary purpose: shaping the massive wooden timbers and tall masts required for the Defias Brotherhood's secret warship. Deep within these subterranean halls, goblin woodcarvers mill and finish raw lumber brought into the mines to construct the rigged vessels of the Brotherhood's hidden fleet.",al={"why is it called mast room","mast room name meaning","why mast room"},it="name",add=true},{q="Is the Mast Room dangerous?",a="Yes. The chamber is heavily guarded by industrious Goblin Woodcarvers and overseen by Sneed, who pilots a lethal goblin shredder against trespassers. Whirling saw blades, heavy logging machinery, and well-armed Defias hirelings make traversing the chamber a hazardous endeavor for anyone who disrupts their carpentry work.",al={"is mast room dangerous","mast room dangers","threats in mast room"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The goblin shredder operated by Sneed in this chamber is a marvel of crude steam-and-cog technology, repurposed from forest logging to crush intruders.",["faction:Alliance"]="The timber processed in this chamber reveals that Defias pillaging across Westfall serves a coordinated industrial effort rather than simple banditry."},kw={"deadmines","goblin woodcarver","lumber mill","mast room","shredder","sneed"},rel={"npc:sneed","zone:deadmines","topic:goblin"},src={"Mast Room"}}
E["zone:deadmines"] = {t="dungeon",n="The Deadmines",z="deadmines",s="Deep beneath the dusty farm town of Moonbrook lies the Deadmines, an enormous subterranean complex that once supplied a third of Stormwind's gold reserves. Abandoned during the First War and long considered haunted, these labyrinthine tunnels have secretly been overtaken by the Defias Brotherhood as their ultimate staging ground. Here, Edwin VanCleef and his conscripted goblin engineers labor away from the eyes of the realm to build an engine of vengeance against the kingdom.",h="Deep beneath the dusty farm town of Moonbrook lies the Deadmines, an enormous subterranean complex that once...",sec={{t="A Legacy of Gold and Ruin",b="Before the First War, the Deadmines were celebrated as the greatest gold-producing center in human lands, financing the prosperity of Stormwind. When the Orcish Horde swept through the kingdom and razed the capital, the mines were hastily abandoned to the dark. During those turbulent years, legendary figures walked these depths: Sir Anduin Lothar was imprisoned by subterranean ogres for twenty months while recovering the sacred Tome of Divinity, and Warchief Blackhand's rebellious daughter Griselda fled into the lower passages alongside the ogre Turok before both met their ends. Believed to be cursed and populated only by shambling undead and lurking subterranean vermin, the depths lay untouched for decades.",sp=0},{t="Sanctum of the Brotherhood",b="When the Stonemasons' Guild was cast out of Stormwind without payment for rebuilding the city, Edwin VanCleef reorganized the disenfranchised artisans into the Defias Brotherhood. Seeking a secure headquarters safe from Gryan Stoutmantle's People's Militia, the thieves established their central redoubt within the abandoned tunnels. They drove out the legitimate Miners' League—leaving Foreman Thistlenettle's doomed workers to perish and rise as undead ghouls—and converted the shafts into an industrial war camp. Guarded by lumbering ogres, seasoned brigands, and mechanical constructs, the lower mines echo once again with picks, fires, and illicit industry.",sp=0},{t="The Secret of Ironclad Cove",b="Beyond the sweltering Goblin Foundry and the timber-strewn Mast Room lies Ironclad Cove, a vast subterranean grotto hollowed out beneath the Dagger Hills. In this hidden harbor, VanCleef has employed goblin shipbuilders and tinkerers to construct a colossal ironclad dreadnaught. Commanded by Captain Greenskin and First Mate Mr. Smite, this warship is engineered to sail through an underwater sea gate leading out toward the ocean, where the Defias Brotherhood means to prey on the sea trade that keeps Stormwind rich.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the entrance to the Deadmines located?",a="The entrance is hidden inside a derelict barn in the ruined town of Moonbrook, located in southwestern Westfall. Winding tunnels pass through an outer complex of Defias diggers and undead miners before reaching the locked instance threshold.",al={"deadmines entrance","how to get to deadmines","where is deadmines"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does everyone call the Deadmines 'VC'?",a="Adventurers frequently refer to the dungeon as 'VC' after its master, Edwin VanCleef. This shorthand is used to avoid confusing the Deadmines with Dire Maul, an ancient elven complex in Feralas that shares the initials 'DM'.",al={"why vc","vc meaning","why call it vc"},it="name"},{q="Who is Edwin VanCleef?",a="Edwin VanCleef was the brilliant guildmaster of the Stonemasons who oversaw the majestic reconstruction of Stormwind City after the First War. When the House of Nobles refused to honor their debts, VanCleef formed the Defias Brotherhood to exact restitution through rebellion and open brigandage.",al={"vancleef backstory","who is the final boss","defias leader"},it="leader"},{q="What is being built in Ironclad Cove?",a="The Defias have contracted goblin engineers to assemble a massive ironclad juggernaught. Armed with heavy ordnance and sturdy timber, the warship is designed to sail out of the cove's sea gate and raid the trade that feeds the capital.",al={"what are they building","deadmines ship","juggernaught"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened to the Miners' League workers outside the instance?",a="Foreman Thistlenettle and his crew were sent to legally reopen the mines for the kingdom. When the Defias stormed the works, a devastating tunnel collapse trapped the miners in the dark, where they starved and eventually rose as mindless, restless undead.",al={"thistlenettle fate","why are there undead miners","collecting memories lore"},it="history"},{q="What does defeating Cookie the murloc mean for the Defias ship?",a="Cookie serves as the bizarre ship's cook aboard VanCleef's dreadnaught. While defeating VanCleef cuts off the head of the rebellion, slaying Cookie cleans out the remaining crew lingering in the ship's galley, utterly breaking the crew's presence in Ironclad Cove before adventurers escape out the coastal passage.",al={"cookie the murloc","why is cookie a boss","cookie deadmines"}},{q="Where does the exit tunnel lead when leaving the dungeon?",a="Following the natural tunnel out behind the dreadnaught brings adventurers to an exit along the coastal bluffs of the Dagger Hills, looking out toward the ocean and the Westfall Lighthouse.",al={"deadmines exit","where does the exit go"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Deadmines?",a="The Deadmines are a sprawling network of labyrinthine tunnels carved deep beneath Westfall and northwestern Stranglethorn Vale. Before the First War, they were the richest gold-producing center in human lands, said to have held a third of Stormwind's entire treasure reserves. They were abandoned when the Horde invaded and sacked the kingdom, leaving the shafts deserted for years until outlaw hands claimed them.",al={"what is the deadmines","deadmines history","tell me about the deadmines"},it="place",add=true,nx={9,10}},{q="Why is it called the Deadmines?",a="After the First War brought devastation and ruin to Stormwind, the abandoned gold shafts fell into dark disuse and were widely believed to be haunted. Between the deadly horrors that prowled their depths and the silence of an exhausted, forsaken realm of stone, travelers began referring to the forsaken pits simply as the Deadmines.",al={"why deadmines named","why called deadmines","deadmines name origin"},it="name",add=true},{q="Who dug these tunnels?",a="Generations of human laborers and guildsmen extracted fortunes of gold from these hills to fuel Stormwind's early expansion. More recently, the Miners' League attempted to reopen the pits under Foreman Thistlenettle, only for the Defias Brotherhood and their conscripted diggers to seize the subterranean network and carve out extensive fortifications of their own.",al={"who built deadmines","who dug deadmines","miners who made deadmines"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Who are the Defias Brotherhood?",a="The Defias Brotherhood is a ruthless order of renegades, bandits, and outlaws made up of former stonemasons, thieves, highwaymen, and cutthroats. Sworn enemies of the kingdom, they have taken control of Westfall and operate from the shadows, plotting to exact bloody vengeance and tear down the ruling nobility of Stormwind.",al={"who are the defias","defias brotherhood","what is defias"},it="threat",add=true,nx={12,13}},{q="Why do they wear red bandanas?",a="The Defias wear red silk bandanas as a defiant symbol of the blood shed by the oppressed working class of Stormwind. It marks their allegiance to Edwin VanCleef's rebellion and reminds every member of the debt of blood they believe the royal court owes them.",al={"why red bandanas","defias red masks","meaning of red bandana"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Who started the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Edwin VanCleef, the former Guildmaster of the Stonemasons Guild, founded the Brotherhood. After spending years rebuilding the shattered ramparts of Stormwind, he turned his extensive training in stealth, subterfuge, and engineering toward open insurrection when the kingdom's aristocracy refused to pay his workers.",al={"who founded defias","who started brotherhood","defias founder"},it="leader",add=true},{q="Why are the Defias hiding in an old mine?",a="The Deadmines offer a massive, defensible fortress hidden beneath the quiet ruins of Moonbrook. With Westfall largely abandoned by the royal army and the tunnels' forgotten subterranean chambers connecting directly to a concealed ocean cove, VanCleef found the perfect secluded staging ground to amass an army and heavy weaponry undisturbed.",al={"why deadmines hideout","why defias in mine","why hide in deadmines"},it="purpose",add=true,nx={15}},{q="Is there really a ship in the mine?",a="Yes. At the deepest point of the labyrinth lies Ironclad Cove, a colossal underground subterranean basin. Anchored there is a massive iron-plated war juggernaught, fitted with heavy cannons and rigged by goblin engineers, ready to sail through a hidden sea gate into the ocean once completed.",al={"is there a ship in deadmines","deadmines juggernaught","defias warship"},it="threat",add=true},{q="Who's in charge down here?",a="Edwin VanCleef commands the entirety of the operation from his cabin aboard the warship deep in Ironclad Cove. From this subterranean perch, he directs the mining, engineering, and raiding operations that grip Westfall.",al={"who leads deadmines","who runs deadmines","deadmines boss"},it="in_charge",add=true,nx={17,18}},{q="Does VanCleef have lieutenants?",a="He commands a diverse cabal of trusted enforcers throughout the shafts. The brutish ogre Rhahk'Zor guards the upper gates, Sneed commands the lumber workshops from within an iron shredder, the goblin Gilnid runs the foundry smelters, and Captain Greenskin alongside the ruthless tauren first mate, Mr. Smite, oversee the juggernaught.",al={"vancleef officers","deadmines commanders","defias lieutenants"},it="allies",add=true},{q="Who are the goblins working for?",a="The goblins work directly under Edwin VanCleef as hired specialists and mercenary craftsmen. Operating the foundry, timber workshops, and shipyards, they bring the technical mastery and industrial machinery needed to construct VanCleef's warmachines in exchange for coin, influence, and resources.",al={"who hired the goblins","are goblins defias","goblin alliance defias"},it="ties",add=true},{q="Why did they send me to kill their leader?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle and the beleaguered People's Militia lack the military strength to breach the Deadmines themselves. With Stormwind turning a blind eye and dismissing the threat, the militia relies entirely on brave, independent adventurers like you to strike deep into the mountain and sever the head of the serpent.",al={"why send me kill vancleef","gryan stoutmantle request","why kill defias leader"},it="why_me",add=true,nx={20,21}},{q="Has anyone else tried to kill VanCleef?",a="Pirates and rival gangs have tried to take what VanCleef holds. A Bloodsail Buccaneer captain named Jerias Bloodvein launched a bloody assault into the tunnels after VanCleef swindled him, cutting down several outposts before mutiny and slaughter tore his pirate crew apart within the depths.",al={"who tried to kill vancleef","past deadmines invasions","did anyone attack deadmines"},it="history",add=true},{q="Why can't the Stormwind army do it?",a="Stormwind's standing forces are stretched thin across Elwynn and distant borders, crippled by debts and bureaucratic apathy. The House of Nobles refuses to fund an expedition to Westfall, leaving the provincial farms undefended and forcing the volunteer People's Militia to handle the crisis alone.",al={"why no stormwind army","why doesnt stormwind clear deadmines","stormwind guards westfall"},it="conflict",add=true},{q="How did the Defias take over the mines?",a="After escaping Stormwind, VanCleef led his followers into the lawless fields of Westfall. They ambushed the local mining operations, murdered the pirate crew that inhabited the coastal cove, collapsed key tunnels to trap royal workers, and fortified the vast underground network into an impregnable base of operations.",al={"how defias took deadmines","how deadmines fell","defias mine takeover"},it="history",add=true,nx={23}},{q="Did the miners join the Defias?",a="While the Miners' League workers were ambushed and perished, many disenfranchised laborers, cutpurses, and desperate vagrants willingly joined the Brotherhood's cause. Today, non-elite laborers and strip miners toil endlessly in the shafts under the watchful whips of Defias overseers and taskmasters.",al={"did miners become defias","are miners defias","miners working for defias"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Why are there goblins down here helping the Defias?",a="Building an armored juggernaught and complex harvest watchers requires advanced metallurgical and mechanical expertise that common bandits lack. VanCleef contracted goblin engineers, craftsmen, and lumber carvers, who happily established foundries and workshops inside the caverns in exchange for wealth and profit.",al={"why goblins deadmines","goblin presence deadmines","why are goblins here"},it="threat",add=true,nx={25,26}},{q="What do the goblins get out of helping the Defias?",a="For the goblins, it is strictly business. They receive a massive cut of gold looted from Westfall's mines, unchecked access to high-grade ore and lumber, and total freedom to test volatile engineering prototypes away from trade prince jurisdiction.",al={"what do goblins get","goblin profit deadmines","why do goblins work for defias"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who is Sneed?",a="Sneed is a cunning goblin supervisor who oversees the Defias lumber operation in the Mast Room. He commands the timber cutting from inside a heavy, razor-edged lumber Shredder, carving massive trees into masts and beams for the dreadnaught.",al={"who is sneed","sneed deadmines","sneed boss"},it="identity",add=true},{q="What is this Stonemasons Guild everyone keeps talking about?",a="The Stonemasons Guild was the esteemed union of architects, masons, and craftsmen led by Edwin VanCleef that rebuilt Stormwind City from ruins following its sacking in the Second War. They restored its white ramparts and towers, only to become the foundation of the rebellion when kingdom politics betrayed them.",al={"stonemasons guild","what was the stonemasons guild","who were the stonemasons"},it="history",add=true,nx={28,29}},{q="Did Stormwind really refuse to pay the Stonemasons?",a="Yes. Stormwind's House of Nobles ran up catastrophic debts expanding military campaigns and refused to provide the full compensation promised for rebuilding the city. Manipulated in secret by Lady Katrana Prestor, the nobility offered only meager payouts and abruptly dissolved the Guild when VanCleef demanded restitution.",al={"did stormwind not pay stonemasons","why werent stonemasons paid","house of nobles payment stonemasons"},sp=1,it="conflict",add=true},{q="Was there a riot in Stormwind?",a="When the guild was disbanded without pay, VanCleef led furious riots through the streets of Stormwind. In the ensuing chaos, King Varian Wrynn's wife, Queen Tiffin, was tragically struck and killed. Grief-stricken and enraged, Varian cracked down harshly, driving the rebellious artisans out into exile.",al={"stormwind riot stonemasons","what happened in the stonemason riot","tiffin wrynn death riot"},sp=1,it="history",add=true},{q="Are the Defias just bandits or something worse?",a="They are far more than common thieves. The Defias Brotherhood is a organized, deeply entrenched revolutionary syndicate wielding advanced goblin engineering, espionage, and trained magic, all driven by a personal and ideological hatred of Stormwind's ruling class.",al={"are defias bandits","how dangerous are defias","defias threat level"},it="threat",add=true,nx={31,32}},{q="Do the Defias have an actual plan?",a="Their goal is nothing short of bringing Stormwind to its knees. By stripping Westfall of resources and starving the capital, while secretly building a heavy iron warship beneath the earth, they intend to sail directly to Stormwind Keep and bombard the kingdom into unconditional surrender.",al={"defias master plan","what is defias goal","what do defias want"},sp=1,it="purpose",add=true},{q="Could the Defias threaten Stormwind itself?",a="Very much so. With King Varian missing, the court paralyzed by internal intrigue, and the royal army stretched past its limit, a surprise naval assault from a fully armed iron juggernaught could shatter Stormwind's harbor defenses and leave the city defenseless from within.",al={"can defias destroy stormwind","could defias take stormwind","threat to stormwind defias"},sp=1,it="danger",add=true},{q="What happens after VanCleef is dead?",a="Delivering VanCleef's severed head to Gryan Stoutmantle at Sentinel Hill confirms the mastermind's demise, dealing a staggering blow to the Brotherhood's grand campaign. Furthermore, documents found upon his corpse, such as an unsent letter, point toward deeper conspiracies and corruption festering in the very heart of Stormwind.",al={"after vancleef dies","vancleef dead what next","fallout of vancleef death"},sp=1,it="next_step",add=true,nx={34,35}},{q="Does killing VanCleef end the Defias?",a="It shatters their immediate plans, but it does not eradicate the rebellion. Thousands of cutpurses, brigands, and sympathizers remain entrenched across Westfall, Redridge, and the Stockades, harboring bitter hatred toward the crown that outlives their founding kingpin.",al={"does defias end with vancleef","is defias defeated","does vancleef death stop defias"},sp=1,it="threat",add=true},{q="Will Westfall finally be safe after VanCleef falls?",a="Not immediately. Rogue mechanical harvest watchers still stalk the blighted fields, gnoll packs prowl the hills, and scattered Defias cells continue to plunder farms. The People's Militia will have a long, uphill struggle before peace ever truly returns to the plains.",al={"is westfall safe now","will westfall recover","westfall after deadmines"},sp=1,it="today",add=true},{q="Why is Westfall such a mess?",a="Westfall was once the fertile breadbasket of the kingdom, but years of neglect, droughts, and Defias terror reduced it to ruin. Outlaws ran off the homesteaders, seized the mines, and left the once-lush pastures fallow and infested with ravenous scavengers and rogue harvest golems.",al={"why is westfall ruined","what happened to westfall","westfall state of affairs"},it="arrival",add=true,nx={37,38}},{q="Where did all the Westfall farmers go?",a="Most were violently driven from their land when the Defias overran the countryside, fleeing to the gates of Sentinel Hill or begging on the streets of Stormwind. Only a handful of stubborn homesteaders remain on their family plots, desperately fighting off bandits and gnolls to scrape together a harvest.",al={"where are the farmers","what happened to westfall farmers","displaced westfall farmers"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Why doesn't the king send help to Westfall?",a="King Varian Wrynn has mysteriously vanished, leaving his young son Anduin and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon to oversee the realm. The royal court, manipulated by squabbling nobles, claims the kingdom has insufficient funds and military manpower to spare for Westfall's defense, abandoning the province to its own devices.",al={"why doesnt the king help westfall","why no help from king","king varian westfall help"},sp=1,it="conflict",add=true},{q="How did I end up in The Deadmines?",a="Your hunt for the Defias Brotherhood led you across the blighted plains of Westfall to Moonbrook, an abandoned town overrun by brigands. A Defias traitor helped you pinpoint their secret headquarters hidden within the dilapidated mine entrance on the edge of town. Fighting your way down through the old mining tunnels and past undead excavations, you breached the depths where the Brotherhood has made its fortified lair.",al={"how did i get here","how did i end up here","how do i get in here"},it="arrival",add=true},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in The Deadmines?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle and the People's Militia sent you to cut the head off the snake. You are here to fight through the Brotherhood's miners, goblin tinkerers, and pirate mercenaries to reach Ironclad Cove. Once there, you must board their warship, confront Edwin VanCleef himself, and claim his head to break the Defias hold over Westfall once and for all.",al={"what am i doing here","what is my goal here","why am i here"},it="purpose",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Deadmines represent the gravest internal threat to the kingdom of Stormwind; bringing down VanCleef is the defining victory that restores hope to the besieged farmers of Westfall.",["class:Paladin"]="These desecrated shafts are a test of valor and faith, echoing the historic trials of Sir Anduin Lothar and the lost miners whose restless dead still wander the outer tunnels.",["profession:Mining"]="Once supplying a third of the capital's wealth, the rocky tunnels remain rich in veins of copper, tin, and precious silver.",["profession:Engineering"]="The Goblin Foundry and Sneed's mechanical workshop offer an inside look at cutting-edge steam shredders, remote-controlled golems, and specialized ordnance."},kw={"cookie","deadmines","defias","edwin vancleef","ironclad cove","juggernaught","moonbrook","mr. smite","vancleef","westfall"},rel={"topic:defias-brotherhood","npc:edwin-vancleef","zone:westfall","subzone:moonbrook","subzone:ironclad-cove","npc:mr-smite","quest:65","quest:373"},m={levels="17-26"},src={"Deadmines (Classic)","Deadmines"}}
